    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Sprayer-Systems-and-Application-Technology-Lead_R19898": {
      "title": "Sprayer Systems and Application Technology Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Sprayer Systems and Application Technology Lead Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 8 years related experience Job Description: Build the Future of Agriculture If you want your work to matter beyond the lab - on real equipment, in real farm fields, with measurable impact - this is the role for you. Who We Are The Digital Ag Innovation Lab at Iowa State University partners with leading agricultural companies to design, build, and deploy next-generation technologies for agriculture. Our team works at the intersection of applied engineering, industry collaboration, and the land-grant mission, moving ideas from concept to prototype to field deployment. Our vision is bold: to be the premiere thought leader and partner in ag innovation . Our mission guides everything we do: Innovate. Educate. Outreach . We operate with four core values: Passion. Innovation. Collaboration. Excellence . This is a place for builders, problem-solvers, and systems thinkers who want their work to move from idea → prototype → field → industry adoption. The Opportunity We are seeking a Sprayer Systems and Application Technology Lead to build and lead a growing program focused on the development, testing, and field evaluation of agricultural application systems.  This role connects application technology, agronomy, and field operations to evaluate how equipment design, application parameters, crop conditions, and management practices affect application performance and agronomic outcomes. This is not a desk-only leadership position.  Successful candidates enjoy spending time in the shop, lab, and field working directly with equipment while also leading people, projects, and sponsor relationships. Working with engineers, agronomists, researchers, and industry partners, you will lead applied research from technical requirements and prototype development through field validation and analysis.  The role combines hands-on engineering, field research, project leadership, and industry collaboration to advance liquid, dry, targeted, and variable-rate application technologies.  What You'll Do Lead development, testing, and field validation of agricultural application systems, including spray, fertilizer, and targeted delivery technologies Define technical and agronomic requirements and develop field and laboratory test methods, performance measures, and validation plans. Evaluate how application systems and operating parameters affect application performance, crop response, input use, and field productivity. Analyze field and system data to guide technology development and improve application performance. Lead and mentor engineers, technicians, students, and research staff while coordinating work across agronomy, engineering, and industry partners. Lead research projects and develop new industry opportunities, including scope, resources, budgets, schedules, sponsor communication, and delivery. What You Bring Experience with agricultural application systems, precision agriculture, agriculture equipment, agronomy, crop production, or related technology development. Working knowledge of agricultural application systems and the engineering principles affecting application performance, such as droplet size, pressure, flow, and speed. Experience with field trials, lab testing, product evaluation, or system benchmarking. Ability to connect engineering performance to agronomic outcomes. Experience leading technical projects, research initiatives, sponsor relationships, and cross-functional teams. Experience with agricultural equipment, agricultural inputs, or production agriculture. Technology & Systems You May Work With Spray systems, nozzles, pumps, and flow control Targeted and variable-rate application technologies Drone and aerial application systems Lab and field-testing platforms Agricultural equipment and precision application systems Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree in agricultural engineering, agronomy, or related field, or equivalent industry experience Background in agriculture application technology, precision agriculture, agricultural equipment, crop input technology, or related industry Experience conducting field trials, in-field testing, or performance benchmarking of ag application systems Experience defining technical requirements, planning test programs, and managing work across cross-functional projects and teams Demonstrated ability to connect engineering parameters (e.g., pressure, droplet size, duty cycle, travel speed) to biological efficacy and input-use efficiency Experience leading or mentoring cross-functional teams in lab and field environments Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. The candidate will be hired as an R&D Engineer IV. https://digitalag.iastate.edu/ Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 1, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS813 Original Posting Date: September 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 20, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19898 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Senior-Spray-Technology-Engineer_R19897": {
      "title": "Senior Spray Technology Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Spray Technology Engineer Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Build the Future of Agriculture If you want your work to move beyond the lab—from concept to prototype to real-world field deployment—while solving complex engineering challenges alongside leading agricultural innovators, this is the role for you. Who We Are The Digital Ag Innovation Lab at Iowa State University partners with leading agricultural companies to design, build, and deploy next-generation technologies for agriculture. Our team works at the intersection of applied engineering, industry collaboration, and the land-grant mission, moving ideas from concept to prototype to field deployment. Our vision is bold: to be the premiere thought leader and partner in ag innovation . Our mission guides everything we do: Innovate. Educate. Outreach . We operate with four core values: Passion. Innovation. Collaboration. Excellence . This is a place for builders, problem-solvers, and systems thinkers who want their work to move from idea → prototype → field → industry adoption. The Opportunity We are seeking a Senior Spray Technology Engineer to lead the technical execution of sponsored research and development projects focused on agricultural application systems. This role combines hands on engineering, field validation, project leadership, and industry collaboration to deliver innovative technologies from concept through field deployment. This is a highly technical, hands-on position for an engineer who enjoys solving complex problems, working directly with agricultural equipment, and leading multidisciplinary project teams. You will collaborate with industry sponsors, researchers, engineers, and students to develop practical solutions that improve application accuracy, efficiency, and agronomic outcomes. This position provides technical and project leadership without formal personnel management responsibilities, allowing the successful candidate to remain focused on engineering, field validation, and sponsor collaboration. What You’ll Do Provide technical leadership for sponsored research projects by coordinating cross-functional teams, guiding engineering decisions, and ensuring successful project execution without formal supervisory responsibility. Lead the design, integration, testing, troubleshooting, and validation of liquid and dry application systems across laboratory and field environments, including ground and aerial platforms. Evaluate application technologies and system performance, including spray nozzles, pumps, flow control, PWM technologies, sensors, and other application hardware, using engineering and field data to improve agronomic outcomes. Collaborate with industry sponsors and project teams to define technical requirements, communicate progress, coordinate engineering, agronomy, technicians, and students, and deliver project objectives. Prepare technical reports, presentations, testing documentation, and project recommendations while supporting proposal development and identifying future research opportunities. Mentor engineers, technicians, and students by providing technical guidance, fostering collaboration, and promoting engineering best practices. What You Bring Experience designing, developing, testing, or validating agricultural application equipment, spray systems, precision agriculture technologies, or related agricultural equipment. Strong mechanical and systems engineering skills, with the ability to troubleshoot complex equipment and evaluate system performance. Experience planning and executing laboratory, field, or product validation testing and translating engineering results into agronomic outcomes and customer value. Demonstrated ability to lead complex technical projects involving multiple stakeholders and collaborate effectively with industry sponsors, researchers, and multidisciplinary teams. Strong organizational skills with the ability to independently manage multiple technical projects while maintaining high standards of safety and quality. Technology & Systems You May Work With Spray systems, nozzles, pumps, and flow control (including PWM) Targeted and variable-rate application technologies Drone and aerial application systems Lab and field-testing platforms Agricultural equipment and precision application systems Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree in Agricultural Engineering, Agronomy, or a related field, or equivalent industry experience. Experience with agricultural application systems through product development, field engineering, technical service, product support, or related roles within agriculture, OEMs, or ag input companies. Experience planning and conducting field trials, performance testing, and validation programs while translating engineering performance into agronomic outcomes. Demonstrated ability to define technical requirements, lead cross-functional technical projects, and mentor engineers, technicians, or project teams. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. The candidate will be hired as an R&D Engineer III. https://digitalag.iastate.edu/ Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 1, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS812 Original Posting Date: September 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 20, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19897 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Crop-Genetic-Resources-and-Informatics_R19903": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Crop Genetic Resources and Informatics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Crop Genetic Resources and Informatics Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking an experienced Postdoctoral Researcher in Crop Genetic Resources and Informatics to apply genome informatics and quantitative genetic approaches to trait analysis in maize. Research will include work on maize pangenomics and population diversity, with opportunities to contribute to similar analyses in other crop systems, including cotton. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Plant Biology Experience conducting population genomic analyses of crop species Experience managing and analyzing large-scale biological datasets Experience using SLURM-based high-performance computing systems Demonstrated proficiency in R Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience obtaining external research funding and/or contributing to funded research projects. Demonstrated experience teaching, training, and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students. Demonstrated record of scholarly productivity, including first-author peer-reviewed publications (minimum of five publications preferred). Demonstrated experience using GitHub or similar platforms for version control, code management, and research data archiving. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively within interdisciplinary research teams and communicate scientific findings through publications and presentations. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology explores everything from how organisms interact with their environment to the interrelationships among species; from the diversity of life to the structure of individual organisms, EEOB provides many ways to study life on our planet.  Department Unit/Website: Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology (EEOB) Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: September 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 11, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19903 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Ames-National-Laboratory_R19911": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ames National Laboratory",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ames National Laboratory Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Division of Materials Science and Engineering is searching for a qualified Postdoctoral Research Associate to conduct experimental research focused on the synthesis, discovery, and characterization of new ferromagnetic materials. The successful candidate will work with Ames National Laboratory scientists, Iowa State University faculty, and external collaborators on a project seeking to identify new permanent magnets. Primary responsibilities will include preparing and conducting high temperature chemical reactions to discover new ferromagnetic materials using techniques such as flux synthesis, arc melting, and powder sintering. The postdoc will analyze the phase and composition of their reaction products using techniques spanning X-ray diffraction, energy dispersive X-ray spectroscopy, electron microscopy, and calorimetry. The postdoc will characterize the physical properties of newly discovered materials, making measurements of their magnetization, electronic transport properties, and specific heat as functions of temperature and applied magnetic field. A major part of the project will also include close collaboration with theoretical and computational materials scientists. The postdoc will perform targeted exploratory reactions in ternary and quaternary compositional spaces to provide experimental benchmarks for computational predictive models. The work will include planning and carrying out experiments, maintaining detailed laboratory records, analyzing data from a diverse range of measurements, and preparing presentations and manuscripts for meetings, conferences, and publications. The ability to work independently, handle multiple tasks, meet milestones, communicate results effectively, and contribute to progress reports is essential. This Postdoctoral Research Associate is a one-year appointment with possibility for renewal. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in condensed matter physics, solid-state chemistry, materials science, or related field Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in condensed matter physics, solid-state chemistry, materials science, or related field Experience with high-temperature solid-state synthesis and crystal growth. Expertise should include techniques such as flux synthesis/solution growth, arc melting, vapor transport reactions, and/or powder sintering. Experience with hot glass-working techniques to prepare and vacuum-seal glass ampoules for conducting reactions. Ability to interpret and construct temperature-composition phase diagrams to guide experimental synthesis efforts. A strong understanding of magnetism and magnetic materials is essential. Experience in measuring and analyzing physical properties including magnetization, electrical resistivity, Hall effect, specific heat, etc. Prior experience operating and maintenance of Quantum Design MPMS and/or PPMS instruments is preferred. Ability to conduct and analyze data from X-ray diffraction measurements, including phase identification and, preferably, Rietveld refinement of powder X-ray diffraction data. Ability to communicate effectively through written reports, oral presentations, manuscripts, and interdisciplinary team discussions. Ability to work collaboratively, maintain accurate laboratory records, and meet project milestones. Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory! Ames Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory. Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Department Unit/Website: www.ameslab.gov   Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: September 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 4, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19911 Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Ames-National-Laboratory_R19826": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ames National Laboratory",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ames National Laboratory Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Division of Materials Science and Engineering seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate to conduct experimental research on superconducting and magnetic quantum materials. The research will emphasize thin and ultrathin films, interfaces, and heterostructures, with particular interest in the superconducting order parameter, thermal and induced quasiparticles, two-level systems, the effects of controlled disorder and emergent phenomena in low-dimensional systems. The materials studied will include superconductors relevant to quantum information science as well as unconventional and candidate topological superconductors and selected magnetic quantum materials. The central research goal is to develop and employ advanced magneto-sensing approaches to identify the mechanisms that cause dissipation and decoherence in superconducting quantum circuits, particularly transmon qubits. The postdoctoral researcher will learn, operate, improve, and help develop custom experimental techniques optimized for small-volume and thin-film samples. This will involve tunnel-diode resonators, real-space magneto-optical imaging, and quantum magneto-sensing using NV centers in diamond. It will also include more conventional thermodynamic and transport measurements. The work will include planning and conducting experiments, critically analyzing experimental results and performing numerical calculations or simulations where appropriate. The researcher must be able to work both independently and collaboratively and to communicate effectively across condensed-matter physics, materials science, and quantum information science. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in experimental condensed-matter physics, materials physics, applied physics, materials science and engineering, or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Strong background in experimental superconductivity, magnetism, and quantum materials, effects of disorder and impurities, and low-dimensional phenomena. Demonstrated hands-on experience with low-temperature experimental techniques, cryogenic systems, vacuum equipment, magnetic fields, low-noise electronics, and precision measurements. Experience with dilution refrigerators and millikelvin measurements is strongly preferred. Experience developing, modifying, or constructing experimental apparatus. Particularly relevant experience includes AC susceptibility, radio- and microwave measurements, magnetic penetration depth, optical magnetometry and magneto-optical imaging. Experience with thin and ultrathin films, interfaces, and heterostructures is highly desirable. Familiarity with conventional materials-characterization techniques and an understanding of the physical information they provide, including transport, PPMS and MPMS measurements, X-ray or neutron scattering, and electron microscopy. Direct experimental expertise in these techniques is not expected. Experience with scientific programming, quantitative data analysis, numerical calculations and simulations using tools such as LabVIEW, Python, MATLAB, Mathematica, Origin, COMSOL Multiphysics, or comparable scientific software. Interest in connecting fundamental materials physics with superconducting quantum information science, in particular the performance of superconducting qubits and microscopic mechanisms of decoherence such as two-level systems, magnetic defects, surfaces, and interfaces. Prior experience working directly with qubits is advantageous but is not required. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in written reports, oral presentations, manuscripts, and interdisciplinary team discussions; collaborate with others; maintain accurate laboratory records; and meet project milestones. Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory! Ames Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Department Unit/Website (if applicable): www.ameslab.gov   Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 2, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 4, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19826 Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Custodian-I---Department-of-Residence_R19111": {
      "title": "Custodian I - Department of Residence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodian I - Department of Residence Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: Are you ready to embark on a custodial role that’s steady, meaningful, and rooted in community? Iowa State University is seeking a dependable and motivated applicants to join the Department of Residence as a Custodian I . You’ll have the opportunity to become a valued member of our campus community; supporting the spaces where students live, study, and connect. As one of the largest non-academic departments on campus, the Department of Residence employs more than 400 staff members who work together to create a supportive learning and social environment for students. In this role, you’ll be at the forefront of maintaining campus buildings and common areas, helping ensure spaces are clean, welcoming, and ready for daily use. Each day brings a mix of routine and variety, offering hands-on work that makes a visible difference. If you’re looking for reliable work, strong benefits, and a team-oriented environment, we encourage you to apply. What You’ll Do Perform general cleaning throughout residence hall buildings, including common areas, restrooms, offices, and other assigned spaces Maintain floors using a variety of methods such as vacuuming, mopping, scrubbing, stripping, and waxing Clean and disinfect bathrooms, fixtures, furniture, and high-touch surfaces Restock supplies such as soap, paper towels, and toilet paper in assigned areas Collect and remove trash and recycling throughout the building Move furniture and equipment as needed to support cleaning and daily operations Assist with basic upkeep such as changing light bulbs and reporting maintenance concerns Support conferences and events by handling linens, room setup, and cleanup as needed Perform limited exterior duties such as clearing entrances, sidewalks, and nearby areas What You’ll Get Insurance benefits beginning on your first day, with timely enrollment. Retirement benefits with strong university contributions. Paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay. Tuition reimbursement available after one year of employment. A collaborative, service-oriented workplace dedicated to supporting students. Preferred Qualifications Prior custodial, janitorial, or commercial cleaning experience Experience operating commercial cleaning equipment Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 0003a Original Posting Date: April 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: October 4, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19111 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Environmental-Systems-Mechanic-II_R19901": {
      "title": "Environmental Systems Mechanic II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Environmental Systems Mechanic II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Six years of experience in temperature and computerized building environmental automation systems, refrigeration or air conditioning work, including apprenticeship, or has two years of experience in computerized building environmental automation systems and meets the minimum eligibility requirements of ESM I; or four years experience in above plus Journeyman’s license; and • Has refrigeration certificate of at least type 2. • May need to possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. • Prefer 2 years of college/trade school. Job Description: Keep critical dining facilities running safely, efficiently, and reliably through skilled maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of essential HVAC, refrigeration, and food service equipment. This position provides comprehensive equipment maintenance and repair support within large-scale dining centers and high-volume food service environments, responding to daily work orders, preventive maintenance needs, and emergency service requests.   The position maintains and repairs commercial refrigeration systems, ice machines, air handling and multi-zone air handling systems, and facility heating and cooling equipment. Responsibilities also include balancing exhaust and supply air systems, monitoring HVAC and refrigeration systems through Metasys, supporting preventive maintenance programs, and communicating repair timelines to management. The position contributes to facility improvements and safety initiatives, documents work through computerized maintenance management systems such as TMA, orders necessary materials and parts, and participates in an on-call rotation to provide after-hours maintenance support. The position also assists with cross-training maintenance staff and performs other duties as assigned. Preferred Qualifications: Experience maintaining commercial HVAC, refrigeration, and food service equipment. Experience troubleshooting ice machines, air handling systems, and heating/cooling equipment. Experience using CMMS and building automation systems such as TMA and Metasys. Knowledge of preventive maintenance, safety standards, and applicable codes. Ability to troubleshoot, prioritize repairs, communicate effectively, and work independently. Learn more about Iowa State University Dining: https://www.dining.iastate.edu Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5091a Original Posting Date: September 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19901 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Cook-II_R19885": {
      "title": "Cook II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Cook II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Two years of experience as a Cook I or outside experience in quantity and quality food preparation comparable thereto. Job Description: Bring great food to life while helping create memorable dining experiences for the ISU community! The Cook II plays an essential role in the daily success of ISU Dining by preparing high-quality meals and menu items according to standardized recipes, production schedules, and food safety procedures. This position performs a variety of complex food production tasks, including preparing meals for regular and special diets, testing food for quality and presentation, and operating a wide range of commercial kitchen equipment. The Cook II helps ensure the kitchen is organized, efficient, and prepared to meet meal period deadlines while maintaining high standards for food quality, safety, sanitation, and customer satisfaction.   The Cook II also provides direction, coaching, and training to student and merit staff, helping coordinate daily kitchen activities and ensuring production and service goals are met. Responsibilities include assisting with employee training and performance activities, monitoring food and equipment temperatures, conducting line and quality checks, and providing friendly customer service. This position also supports inventory and supply management by requisitioning, receiving, storing, labeling, dating, and rotating food products; recording leftovers; and assisting with inventory procedures. The Cook II contributes to a clean, safe, and welcoming dining environment and may assist with recipe testing, development, and other operational needs as assigned. Schedule: Monday-Thursday 11:30AM - 8:00PM, Saturday 5:30AM - 2:00PM. Hours may vary based on operating needs. Nights and weekends as needed.   What You Can Expect Insurance benefits (medical, dental, and vision) starting on your first day Retirement plans with generous university contributions A free meal with every shift Paid time off , sick leave, and holiday pay — enjoy holidays off The opportunity to influence how food is prepared and served across campus   Preferred Qualifications: Commercial cooking experience Food safety & sanitation Recipe/production schedule compliance Staff training & leadership Commercial kitchen equipment & inventory management About ISU Dining ISU Dining is a nationally recognized campus dining program committed to culinary innovation and excellent service. From residential dining centers and cafés to catering and retail outlets, we serve thousands daily, offering variety, consistency, and quality. This position plays a key role behind the scenes, ensuring every meal starts with a strong foundation.   As a member of the dining team, you’ll be part of a fast-paced, high-volume kitchen unlike anything most have experienced. Every day is different as you help manage large-scale meal prep, fine-tune recipes, and keep things running smoothly. If you enjoy leading a team, learning on the job, and working with talented students and full-time workers, this role could be a perfect fit! Watch Our Team in Action! Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 07 Original Posting Date: September 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19885 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Carpenter_R19879": {
      "title": "Carpenter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Carpenter Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Four years of experience in the trade, including apprenticeship. Job Description: Iowa State University is seeking a skilled carpenter to join our team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for maintaining and enhancing the physical environment of our residence halls. This role involves performing a variety of carpentry tasks, including repairs, installations, and construction projects, to ensure a safe and comfortable living space for our students. The carpenter will work closely with other staff members to support the overall mission of the Department of Residence. Under general supervision, applies knowledge and skill at the level of a journeyworker to build and repair wooden and related structures, and performs other duties related or incidental thereto. Preferred Qualifications: Experience installing wood or vinyl flooring. Experience hanging and finishing sheet rock. Finished cabinet making experience. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Constructs, installs, and repairs cabinets, doors, windows, screens, shades, blinds, furniture, seats, laminate materials and other components not available from commercial sources.   • Constructs walls, ceilings and floors. Frames and installs doors and windows; insulates walls and performs demolition work as necessary.   • Estimates, measures, fabricates and cuts metals for associated jobs using precision leveling equipment. Design and fabricate necessary metal and wood projects that do not necessarily have a planned design.  Fabricate one-off pieces to include, but not limited to: brackets, hangers, supports, etc.  • Lays tile, linoleum, laminates, epoxies and various other kinds of coverings on floors and other surfaces; patches, repairs or replaces work and damaged floors; installs counter tops and covers other surfaces; cuts forms and adheres coverings to various shapes and types of surface; tapes and finishes dry wall.   • Installs door closures, hinges, door stops, handles, related hardware and performs minor glazing.  • Performs patching, repair and rust removal work for all types of walls and surfaces to a finished stage.  Full and partial removal of existing materials like door frames, cutting and final fitment of replacement parts, then surface preparation to provide smooth finished texture with tasks such as grinding, sanding, body filler and primer for final finishes and applies finishes as required.  • Draws rough layouts and reads and interprets blueprints and drawings. • Prepare estimates of materials and time needed to complete assigned jobs and orders materials as needed.  • Erects and disassembles ladders and related equipment.  • Assembles and disassembles all supports, structure, hangers, mounts (motorized or non-motorized) for audio visual equipment installations including ergonomic workstations.  May also rework existing building structure to allow for new or replacement projection screens.  • Set up and tear down of office spaces. Ability to assemble and disassemble different types of modular office furniture.  Includes walls (with or without power and data capabilities), doors, shelves, desks, filing cabinets, etc.  Ability to recognize different manufacturers and their unique assembly requirements.  • Assists in directing work and training of apprentices and other workers.  Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the principles, methods and techniques used in the carpentry trade. • Ability to perform the full range of carpentry tasks independently. • Ability to interpret and follow carpentry instructions and specifications such as blueprints, manuals, sketches, and work orders.   • Ability to operate safely and care for carpentry tools, machines and equipment. • Knowledge of materials used in carpentry and ability to determine materials needed for the job and prepare cost estimates.   • Ability to lift or maneuver up to 100 pounds.   • Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade.   • Ability to erect ladders and work at heights.  • Knowledge and working ability of computers for planning, organizing and ordering equipment and materials.  • Ability to set up and tear down audiovisual equipment.  • Knowledge of standard cleaning techniques, rust removal techniques, and characteristics of surfaces to be cleaned, and equipment and supplies required.  Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position . Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5061a Original Posting Date: September 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 17, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19879 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Project-Coordinator---Temporary_R19888": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator - Temporary",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Project Coordinator - Temporary Appointment Type: Professional & Scientific Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities The Food Science and Human Nutrition Department in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences is seeking applicants for a temporary project coordinator to: Follow up on communication with Polymer and Food Protection Consortium (PFPC) members Track member projects Track projects and deadlines from intake to completion Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelors degree Preferred Qualifications Experience with plastic and polymer packaging testing Department/Program & College Description The Polymer and Food Protection Consortium at Iowa State University conducts industry‑relevant research to develop innovative solutions that improve the design, safety, and functionality of materials used in packaging and industrial applications. Through a combination of fundamental and applied research, the consortium supports industry partners and actively drives knowledge and technology transfer to help address real‑world challenges in packaging, materials performance, and food safety. Department Unit/Website Polymer and Food Protection Consortium Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: September 14, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: P&S Temporary Original Posting Date: September 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19888 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-Biomedical-Sciences_R19889": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track Assistant Professor Biomedical Sciences Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Biomedical Sciences at the Iowa State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor. These are full-time, 9-month positions with salary commensurate with qualifications. The successful candidates will join a department with active research programs in pharmacology, neuroscience, vaccine development, infectious disease, and molecular and cell biology. These individuals will be expected to establish a dynamic, extramurally-funded research program within these or a complementary field pertinent to human and/or animal health. The successful candidates will also teach pharmacology to professional and/or graduate students. Research programs in pharmacology-relevant disciplines are of particular interest, including neurobiology, cellular signaling, drug mechanism and mode of action, endocrinology, toxicology, and receptor or antimicrobial pharmacology.   Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD with research experience relevant to Biomedical Sciences Preferred Qualifications: Research plans and experience relevant to Pharmacology or other Biomedical Sciences Strong record of publication in peer-reviewed journals relative to appointment Demonstrated success obtaining extramural funding Evidence of effective research mentoring experience Teaching engagement at a university or professional school Department/Program & College Description: The Biomedical Sciences department supports the mission of the College of Veterinary Medicine by teaching a basic science curriculum to veterinary medical students, conducting state-of-the-art basic and translational research relevant to the health of animals and humans, and educating graduate students through both the departmental graduate program and several multidisciplinary interdepartmental programs at Iowa State University. Departmental faculty research programs span a range of One Health disciplines including pharmacology, neuroscience, microbial and helminth infectious disease and vaccine development. Iowa State University and Central Iowa Iowa State University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 institution with a student enrollment exceeding 30,000 located in Ames, a progressive community just 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest . More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/bms/ https://vetmed.iastate.edu/about/about-the-college/cvm-employment/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Cover Letter 2) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 3) Research Statement detailing past accomplishments and future goals (3 pages maximum) 4) Teaching Statement detailing pedagogy, experience and future plans (1 page maximum) 5) Contact information for Three Professional References external to Iowa State University If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before October 05, 2026. This position will be open until filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: September 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19889 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Veterinary-Technician-I_R19892": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Veterinary Technician I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Associate or Bachelor’s degree in a veterinary technology program accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or the Canadian Veterinary Medical Association (CVMA), and • Registered, licensed, or certified as a veterinary technician within one year of the start date. Job Description: Whether you're launching your veterinary technician career or looking to advance your expertise in a specialty area, the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center offers the opportunity to grow your skills, work alongside leading specialists, and make a meaningful impact on animal health.  The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) at Iowa State University is seeking Veterinary Technicians to join our team. We are hiring across multiple specialty areas, including Emergency & Critical Care, Anesthesia, and the Large Animal Hospital.  As Iowa's premier veterinary teaching hospital, the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center provides advanced medical and surgical care for companion and large animals from across Iowa and the surrounding region. Our board-certified specialists, residents, interns, veterinary technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work together to deliver exceptional patient care while advancing veterinary medicine through education, research, and clinical excellence.  Apply once and be considered for multiple Veterinary Technician opportunities across Emergency & Critical Care, Anesthesia, and the Large Animal Hospital.  Successful candidates hired into a Veterinary Technician I, II, or III position within Emergency & Critical Care, Anesthesia, or the Large Animal Hospital between May 1, 2026 and June 30, 2027 may be eligible for a $1,000 recruitment incentive. Payment terms and conditions will be outlined in a payment agreement at the time of hire.  Why Join the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center?  At Iowa's premier veterinary teaching hospital, you'll be part of a collaborative team dedicated to exceptional patient care, education, and innovation. Working alongside board-certified specialists, clinicians, residents, interns, and veterinary students, you'll gain hands-on experience with advanced medical and surgical cases while continuing to develop your technical and clinical skills.  Whether your passion is emergency medicine, anesthesia, or large animal care, you'll have the opportunity to make a direct impact on patient outcomes while helping educate the next generation of veterinarians.  What You'll Do  Responsibilities vary by specialty area but may include:  Provide compassionate, high-quality nursing care to hospitalized, emergency, critical care, and surgical patients.  Perform veterinary technical procedures under the direction of licensed veterinarians.  Monitor patient status, recognize changes in condition, and communicate findings to the veterinary team.  Administer medications, treatments, and fluid therapy.  Assist with emergency procedures, anesthesia, surgery, diagnostics, and patient recovery.  Collect and process diagnostic samples.  Safely handle and restrain companion and/or large animal patients.  Operate, maintain, and troubleshoot specialized medical equipment.  Maintain accurate and thorough medical records.  Collaborate with faculty clinicians, residents, interns, veterinary students, and fellow technicians to coordinate patient care.  Demonstrate clinical techniques and support the educational experience of veterinary students.  Specialty Areas: Emergency & Critical Care (ECC)  Provide nursing care for emergency and critically ill patients in a fast-paced environment that delivers advanced care 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. Technicians play an essential role in triaging patients, supporting emergency procedures, and providing continuous monitoring for hospitalized patients.  Anesthesia  Support all phases of anesthesia, including patient assessment, anesthetic preparation, induction, monitoring, pain management, and recovery while working alongside board-certified anesthesiologists and experienced anesthesia technicians.  Large Animal Hospital  Support the care of equine and food animal patients in emergency, intensive care, medical, and surgical settings. Technicians work closely with clinicians and students to provide comprehensive patient care while developing advanced large animal nursing and technical skills.  Work Environment  These positions are fully onsite at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center and involve hands-on patient care in a collaborative clinical environment. Depending on the specialty area, schedules may include rotating shifts, on-call responsibilities, weekends, holidays, and physically active work with companion and/or large animal patients. Candidates in positions requiring on-call coverage must live within a reasonable distance of the hospital to meet response-time expectations.  Preferred Qualifications Experience working with small and/or large animal patients in a veterinary clinical setting. Experience in a veterinary teaching hospital, specialty/referral hospital, or high-volume general practice, including completion of clinical rotations in these settings. Experience providing nursing care to veterinary patients, including patient restraint, handling, monitoring, and treatment in emergency, anesthesia, medical, or surgical environments. Experience assisting with anesthesia, surgical procedures, emergency and critical care, or large animal procedures, including patient monitoring and recovery. Experience performing technical skills such as venipuncture, intravenous (IV) catheter placement, medication administration, collection of diagnostic samples, and operation of common veterinary equipment under appropriate supervision. . Department Unit/Website: http://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/ Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 7601a Original Posting Date: September 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 30, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19892 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Learning-and-Development-Specialist-I_R19881": {
      "title": "Learning and Development Specialist I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Learning and Development Specialist I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: Help people succeed from their first day to their last—and strengthen the systems that support them along the way. The Learning & Development Specialist I supports ISU Dining’s employee onboarding, training, and development programs. Under the guidance of the Quality Assurance Specialist II, this role coordinates orientation and onboarding activities, facilitates and coordinates training, manages training assignments and records, updates training content, and serves as a resource to employees and managers on policies, procedures, expectations, and organizational culture. This role works closely with ISU Dining employees, managers, supervisors, and other partners to coordinate training and identify, develop, and improve learning programs. Responsibilities include monitoring trainings, auditing records, maintaining current training materials, uploading content and enrolling employees in trainings, and coordinating in-person training. The position also provides support for food safety, workplace safety, PPE and chemical programs, facility audits and inspections, incident investigations, and compliance with applicable food safety and OSHA standards. ServSafe Food Protection Manager Certification is required within six months. Preferred Qualifications: Experience coordinating or facilitating employee training and onboarding programs. Experience with food safety, sanitation, quality assurance, or compliance. Experience with learning technologies and training record systems. Experience coordinating across multiple departments and stakeholders. About the Department: ISU Dining is at the heart of campus life, serving thousands of students, faculty, staff, and guests across Iowa State University. With a focus on quality, service, safety, and innovation, ISU Dining provides a wide range of dining experiences while creating a welcoming environment for employees and the campus community. Our team supports student success through great food and service while providing employees with opportunities to learn, grow, and build meaningful careers in foodservice. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: September 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 16, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19881 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
