    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Administrative-Assistant-II_R19863": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Administrative Assistant II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: The Debbie and Jerry Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University is seeking an Administrative Assistant II to support the Departments of Supply Chain Management and Management & Entrepreneurship. This position is ideal for a highly organized, proactive professional who thrives in a fast-paced, customer-focused environment. Reporting to two Department Chairs, the Administrative Assistant II provides executive-level administrative support and helps ensure the efficient day-to-day operations of both departments. The successful candidate will serve as the primary point of contact for faculty, staff, students, alumni, and external partners, delivering exceptional customer service while managing multiple priorities with professionalism and discretion. The ideal candidate will possess strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills, a service-oriented mindset, and proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Outlook, and Word. Experience with Workday or similar enterprise systems is preferred, along with the ability to quickly learn new technologies. Example of Duties Served as the primary administrative liaison for department leadership, coordinating operations, communications, and strategic initiatives. Managed calendars, meetings, and departmental events, including symposiums, advisory council meetings, and faculty meetings. Prepared reports and analyzed enrollment and course data to support departmental planning, budgeting, and decision-making. Provided guidance on university policies, budgets, HR matters, and administrative procedures to department leadership. Coordinated faculty recruitment, search processes, promotion and tenure activities, and maintained confidential personnel records. Oversaw hiring and supervision of student employees and tracked faculty and staff leave. Developed departmental communications, newsletters, website content, and correspondence for internal and external stakeholders. Served as the first point of contact for faculty, students, visitors, and campus partners, delivering professional customer service. Collaborated across departments to support academic programs, organizational goals, and continuous process improvement. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to deliver exceptional customer service as the primary point of contact for internal and external stakeholders. Experience managing calendars, scheduling meetings, and coordinating departmental events and logistics. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, specifically Excel, Outlook, and Word. Demonstrated ability to independently manage responsibilities, prioritize competing tasks, and consistently meet deadlines. Experience working collaboratively across departments while demonstrating strong organizational skills, professionalism, and attention to detail. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: September 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19863 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-or-Clinical-Track---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Anesthesiology_R19820": {
      "title": "Tenure or Clinical Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Anesthesiology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure or Clinical Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Anesthesiology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University (ISU) is seeking qualified applicants for a full time, clinical or tenure track faculty appointment in Anesthesiology in the Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) and the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The LVMC is a state-of-the-art teaching hospital providing specialized care for companion and production animals throughout Iowa and the surrounding states. The candidates will join an anesthesia team comprised of 3 faculty Anesthesiologists that are complemented by 9 veterinary anesthesia technicians and 1 anesthesia residents. The department is seeking candidates to provide excellent patient care, teach didactic and laboratory courses in veterinary anesthesiology, provide clinical training for technicians and house officers, and enhance the national prominence of the LVMC’s Anesthesiology section. The successful candidate will help develop creative programs in scholarship, didactic and laboratory teaching in anesthesiology, academic service, and outreach activities. Clinical duties will include weekends, holidays, and after-hours service that are shared amongst the anesthesia faculty. Please elaborate on your ability to meet these preferred qualifications in your application. Start date is negotiable depending on the candidate. Second and third year ACVAA/ECVAA residents are encouraged to apply.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Successful completion of an American College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ACVAA) or European College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ECVAA) residency program before first day of employment. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment. Preferred Qualifications: Diplomate of the American College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (DACVAA) . Experience working with veterinary technicians and/or veterinary students in a clinical teaching setting. Experience running a clinical anesthesia service with a moderate to high caseload. Please elaborate on your ability to meet these preferred qualifications in your application. Department/Program & College Description: The LVMC is a state-of-the-art facility designed to provide specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients. As the nation’s first public veterinary school, Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine takes pride in its heritage while shaping the future of veterinary professional practice, education, research and service. At Iowa State, we translate our core values into action by seeking individuals who have experience working with students, colleagues, and constituents in various settings while performing to a high standard. Ames, Iowa is a progressive community of 60,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines, and has been named one of the best college towns in the nation with much to do and discover.   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/small-animal/support-services/anesthesiology/ https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before September 24, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 25, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19820 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Animal-Welfare-and-Food-Animal-Medicine_R19873": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Animal Welfare and Food Animal Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Animal Welfare and Food Animal Medicine Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will support VDPAM's missions in teaching, research, and clinical service. Responsibilities include contributing to instruction in animal welfare, animal handling, and clinical medicine; supporting animal welfare research projects; and providing clinical support to food animal veterinary units. The position also includes participation in emergency service and up to 20% of the on-call duty rotation for the Food Animal Veterinary Field Services unit. Required Minimum Qualifications: Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) degree with two or more years of food animal veterinary experience PhD with an emphasis in animal welfare, awarded by the position start date Must have an IA license to practice veterinary, USDA category II accreditation & ability to acquire controlled drug licenses Must have a valid US Driver's License. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching veterinary students in a food animal clinical setting. Research experience in animal welfare.   Department/Program & College Description: At VDPAM, we lead the future of food animal and population medicine. As a global center of excellence, we are recognized for our expertise, valued for our collaborative partnerships, and trusted to deliver innovative, science-driven solutions to the most pressing challenges in animal health and food production. We advance our vision by empowering current and future veterinarians, scientists, and industry stakeholders through exceptional education, groundbreaking research, and world-class clinical and diagnostic services. Every day, we work to elevate animal health, enhance productivity and welfare, strengthen food safety, and support a sustainable global food system. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Diagnostic and Production Animal Medicine - Veterinary Diagnostic and Production Animal Medicine Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: September 21, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: September 1, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 7, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19873 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Communications-Specialist-Temporary_R19876": {
      "title": "Communications Specialist Temporary",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Communications Specialist Temporary Appointment Type: Professional & Scientific Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Iowa Pork Industry Center (IPIC) provides swine producer education and outreach based on university research and producer needs. The Communication Specialist will support these efforts by creating web and social media content, success stories, monthly newsletters, and other communication materials that translate research findings into practical, producer-focused information. The position will work closely with faculty, researchers, and industry stakeholders to communicate scientific information in a clear, engaging, and accessible manner for pork producers and other audiences. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications: - Bachelor's degree in a science related field - Website development and content creation experience - Experience in developing short communications (i.e. infographics, fact sheets)   Department/Program & College Description: The Iowa Pork Industry Center (IPIC) provides research-based education and outreach to pork producers and industry stakeholders. By connecting university research with producer needs, IPIC develops and delivers practical resources, training, and educational programs that support a sustainable and innovative swine industry. Department Unit/Website: Iowa Pork Industry Center | Iowa State University Extension and Outreach Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: September 21, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: P&S Temporary Original Posting Date: September 1, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 11, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19876 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Financial-Aid-Advisor-II_R19749": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Financial Aid Advisor II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Help students turn financial aid into a path toward achieving their educational goals. As a Financial Aid Advisor II , you’ll guide students and families through financial aid options, applications, awards, scholarships, eligibility requirements, and policies. You’ll provide individualized advising and financial literacy support while handling more in-depth financial aid processing to ensure students receive accurate and timely assistance. You’ll also help maintain compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations while supporting the administration of federal, state, and private aid programs. In this role, you’ll review student eligibility and adjust financial aid packages, resolve account holds, monitor enrollment and withdrawal activity, coordinate outside aid, and maintain federal financial aid systems such as Federal Student Aid, COD, and NSLDS. You’ll also provide individual advising and group presentations to help students and families better understand their financial aid and financial literacy resources. We’re looking for a student-focused, detail-oriented financial aid professional who can navigate complex regulations while providing exceptional service to students and families. The ideal candidate has experience administering financial aid programs, interpreting financial aid policies and regulations, and using financial aid systems and processing tools. Strong problem-solving, analytical, organizational, and communication skills are essential, along with the ability to manage multiple priorities and work effectively both independently and as part of a team. This is a one-year term position, with the potential for renewal based on funding availability. About the Department: The Office of Student Financial Aid at Iowa State University is committed to empowering over 85% of undergraduate students through the administration of more than $400 million in financial assistance annually. As a unit within the Division of Academic Affairs, our team helps students and their families understand, apply for, and manage financial aid throughout their academic journey. We are driven by values of student success, innovation, collaboration, and respect. Our supportive work environment emphasizes personal and professional growth, with opportunities for training, development, and meaningful contributions to the university’s mission. Join us in making college more accessible and affordable for Iowa State students. Preferred Qualifications: Experience administering federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs. Experience using Federal Student Aid, COD, NSLDS, or other financial aid systems. Experience interpreting and applying federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations and policies. Experience providing financial aid advising and counseling to students and families. Experience with financial aid processing, including eligibility review, award adjustments, account holds, and outside aid coordination. Analytical and problem-solving skills Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: September 21, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: August 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19749 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Diagnostic-Associate-I_R19869": {
      "title": "Diagnostic Associate I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Diagnostic Associate I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Special Required Qualifications Must have accurate color recognition (Inactive) Job Description: The Iowa State University Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory (VDL) is seeking a Diagnostic Associate I to join our Molecular Diagnostics team. As one of the nation's leading veterinary diagnostic laboratories, the VDL processes more than 127,000 diagnostic cases and performs over 1.7 million tests annually , providing critical diagnostic and surveillance services for veterinarians, producers, researchers, and government agencies across the country. In this role, you'll perform molecular diagnostic testing that helps identify and monitor diseases affecting livestock, poultry, and other animal populations. Whether supporting routine diagnostics or assisting with disease surveillance programs, your work will contribute to timely decision-making that protects animal agriculture and public health. What You'll Do As a Diagnostic Associate I, you will: Perform molecular diagnostic testing including DNA/RNA extraction, conventional PCR, real-time PCR, and quantitative PCR (qPCR). Process and evaluate incoming samples, verify quality controls, analyze test results, and release results following training and demonstrated proficiency. Support surveillance and monitoring programs through high-quality laboratory testing and analysis. Assist with laboratory quality assurance and quality control activities, including determining sample suitability and troubleshooting testing issues. Contribute to research and development projects focused on diagnostic test improvement and validation. Preferred Qualifications Hands-on experience performing DNA and/or RNA extraction in a laboratory setting. Experience conducting PCR, real-time PCR, and/or quantitative PCR (qPCR) testing. Experience working in a diagnostic, clinical, veterinary, public health, or research laboratory. Experience following laboratory quality assurance and quality control (QA/QC) procedures. Experience processing high-volume biological samples and/or using a laboratory information management system (LIMS). What We're Looking For We're seeking someone who: Pays close attention to detail and takes pride in producing accurate work. Can identify and troubleshoot unexpected results. Works well independently while also collaborating with laboratory colleagues. Stays organized and productive in a fast-paced environment. Communicates effectively and maintains a commitment to quality and safety. Additional Information Full-time, regular position. Monday through Friday schedule. Work is performed in a veterinary diagnostic laboratory environment and includes handling biological specimens and working with laboratory instrumentation. Accurate color recognition is required to evaluate samples, quality controls, and diagnostic test results. About the Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory The Iowa State University Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory (VDL) provides advanced diagnostic testing, disease surveillance, and research support for veterinarians, livestock producers, animal owners, industry partners, and government agencies. As one of the nation's leading veterinary diagnostic laboratories, the VDL plays a critical role in protecting animal health, supporting food security, and advancing scientific discovery through high-quality diagnostic services and research. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: August 31, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19869 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Lennox-AV-Preservation-Librarian_R19847": {
      "title": "Lennox AV Preservation Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Lennox AV Preservation Librarian Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree Job Description: The Iowa State University Library is seeking applications for a Lennox AV Preservation Librarian (Librarian I) who will support the library in maintaining long-term access to unique and rare sound recordings and moving image collections. This is a new, full-time term position that is funded by both the Col. Gary G. Swenson Ph.D. endowment and the Lennox Foundation endowment for one year. As a member of the Preservation department, they will work closely with other members in support of the mission and vision of the division: to provide long-term access to evolving collections and collaborate in the creation of new knowledge. The Lennox AV Preservation Librarian is primarily responsible for assisting in the maintenance and care of the Special Collections & University Archives (SCUA) audiovisual collections and digital conversion of AV and film materials. In cooperation with SCUA and Preservation staff, this role will be instrumental in implementing preservation and digitization priorities for the collection. They will work with vendors and manage digital conversion projects, provide recommendations for preservation storage for both analog and digital masters, and assist in incorporating AV materials into the library digital collections. The Lennox AV Preservation Librarian may help manage equipment to facilitate reformatting and playback of analog AV collections. The successful candidate will have experience with archival audiovisual collections and will provide preservation care, handling, conversion of AV materials to digital formats, and recommending digital preservation and storage practices. The candidate will possess the ability to interact effectively with library staff and the university community and work collaboratively in a team-based environment. This position will perform physical activities associated with preservation environments which include regular lifting of up to 40lbs. and moving loaded book trucks weighing up to 300 lbs. This position also responds to disaster salvage of library materials and will be an active member in fulfilling the land-grant mission of the university by participating in state-level disaster response as needed. The library is committed to supporting all librarians through mentoring, training, and professional development opportunities to foster success and growth in their work. The Lennox AV Preservation Librarian will be supported in the pursuit of continued learning relevant to their position and encouraged to share their skills with their colleagues at ISU and beyond. Example of Duties: Assist with managing film and audiovisual collection storage. Conduct surveys and assessments of AV materials. Develop and manage projects for rehousing, inventory, and storage. Support environmental monitoring and integrated pest management. Collect and report AV preservation statistics. Collaborate across library departments to support collection goals. Assist with disaster preparedness, salvage, and recovery activities. Coordinate and prepare materials for reformatting and digitization projects. Perform quality control for in-house and vendor digitization projects. Research and recommend preservation specifications for physical and digital AV materials. Evaluate and assist with hardware and digitization software. Create and maintain appropriate administrative and descriptive metadata. Maintain audiovisual studios and equipment, including installation, repairs, and upgrades. Recommend preservation formats and long-term storage solutions for digital AV materials. Prepare digitized media for access and fulfill reference and research requests. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with digital and analog audiovisual formats, technologies, and standards and best practices for preservation, storage, digitization, playback, and access. Previous experience handling and transferring archival film, sound, and video recordings, and working with third-party vendors. Ability to operate and perform basic troubleshooting for a variety of AV playback and scanning equipment. Demonstrated ability to work independently as well as effectively in a collaborative team environment. Demonstrated ability to manage projects of limited scope and complexity. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, please apply before September 15th, 2026. This position is a one-year term appointment. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: January 3, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: August 31, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19847 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
