    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Cook-I_R19550": {
      "title": "Cook I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Cook I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: Iowa State University Dining is seeking enthusiastic individuals to join our team as Cook I across multiple campus dining locations. These positions will be 9, 10, 11 and 12 month opportunities with varies schedules offered. This is a great opportunity for those with experience in food service, hospitality, or customer-facing roles who enjoy hands-on kitchen work and want to build their skills in a steady, team-focused environment. At ISU Dining, you’ll work alongside a dedicated group of culinary professionals in one of the largest dining programs in the country. With more than 20 dining locations on campus, our teams prepare fresh, high-quality food while supporting daily campus life. Positions may support a variety of service areas, including residential dining, retail locations, and catering operations. Learn more about Iowa State University Dining: https://www.dining.iastate.edu What You’ll Do Prepare and cook food by following recipes and production guidelines for a variety of menu items. Support service operations by assisting with daily meal service and/or catering events, as assigned. Maintain food safety standards by following proper sanitation, safety, and temperature requirements. Assist with training and team support by helping guide student employees and supporting coworkers during service. Handle supplies and inventory by monitoring food and supply needs and assisting with deliveries. Keep work areas clean and organized by maintaining kitchen equipment, utensils, and prep spaces. What You’ll Get Insurance benefits beginning on your first day, with timely enrollment. Retirement benefits with strong university contributions. Paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay. Tuition reimbursement available after one year of employment. Free meals provided during scheduled work shifts. A collaborative, service-oriented workplace dedicated to supporting students. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities Prepares and cooks meats, fish, vegetables, gravies, cereals, soups, fruits, bakery products and other forms of food. Prepares and cooks food for special diets from recipes formulated by qualified personnel. Assists in on-the-job training and assists in directing the work of food service workers, students and other employees within area of assignment. Assists in the preparation of salads and desserts. Notifies supervisor of food and supplies needed. Checks in food and supplies as necessary. Maintains food production records. Cleans kitchen, kitchen utensils and equipment; secures refrigerator and freezer. Serves food as required. Maintains maximum standards of sanitation and safety. Performs other related duties and responsibilities as required or assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to judge final food product for quantity (yield) and quality (color, taste, texture, etc.). Ability to determine the freshness and quality of raw and cooked food products by sight and taste. Knowledge of safe temperatures for serving food and storage of refrigerated and frozen storage of raw and cooked foods. Knowledge of principles of food sanitation, health hazards, and the necessary precautionary measures. Ability to stand for long periods of time. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Ability to provide on-the-job training in food preparation to lower level employees. Ability to maintain effective working relationships with others. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 0004a Original Posting Date: June 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19550 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Building-Services-Specialist-II_R19837": {
      "title": "Building Services Specialist II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Building Services Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Summary Are you an experienced, hands-on professional who wants to help students create, make, and innovate?  The Student Innovation Center is seeking qualified candidates for a Building Services Specialist II who will provide supervision, coordination, customer service, and equipment management in the Second level of the center for the Electronics, Textiles, and 3D Printing makerspace. Key Responsibilities Makerspace Coordination: Implement and enforce safety standards and protocols. Coordinate student access and usage of the makerspace. Develop and implement best practices for training and supervision of equipment use. Maintain records related to makerspace activities, equipment usage, and student engagement. Manage makerspace resources and communicate additional needs to leadership. Equipment Management: Oversee general equipment upkeep, troubleshoot issues, and perform basic repairs. Maintain a functional, clean, and organized makerspace environment. Develop and implement training procedures and guidelines for proper equipment use. Provide support for student projects and requests related to electronics, textiles, and 3D printing. Continuously enhance personal skills and knowledge in makerspace technologies. Ensure security and proper handling of makerspace tools and equipment. Customer Service & Community Engagement: Create a welcoming environment for all users. Maintain high standards of professional ethics and relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Plan and participate in workshops, events, and outreach activities that promote the makerspace. Provide professional presentations and training sessions to showcase the capabilities of the Student Innovation Center. Maintain effective communication with managers, stakeholders, and makerspace users.     Additional information:  Work schedule is Wednesday - Saturday, 9:00am to 8:00PM. Preferred Qualifications Strong supervisory experience Previous experience providing hands-on training Experience developing, implementing, and enforcing safety standards and standard operating procedures for equipment Direct experience working with students, faculty, and staff Experience with equipment setup, programming, operating, troubleshooting, maintenance, and repair For more information about the Student Innovation Center, please visit: Student Innovation Center – Iowa State University Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: August 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 10, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19837 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Veterinary-Technician_R19859": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Veterinary Technician Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Associate or Bachelor’s degree in a veterinary technology program accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or the Canadian Veterinary Medical Association (CVMA), and • Registered, licensed, or certified as a veterinary technician within one year of the start date. Special Required Qualifications Valid U.S. Driver's License Job Description: Are you interested in supporting innovative research while promoting the highest standards of animal health and welfare? Laboratory Animal Resources at Iowa State University is seeking a Veterinary Technician to provide clinical and technical support for a variety of laboratory animal species used in research and teaching programs, including rodents, swine, sheep, cattle, and other agricultural and research animals. In this role, you will work closely with veterinarians, researchers, and animal care staff to support animal health programs, medical procedures, research activities, and regulatory compliance. This position is ideal for someone who enjoys applying their veterinary technician skills in a collaborative research environment where their work directly contributes to scientific discovery and advancement. What You'll Do Provide clinical care for laboratory animals through medication administration, health monitoring, catheter placement and maintenance, treatment support, and patient recovery activities. Assist veterinarians and researchers with medical and surgical procedures, including anesthesia monitoring, sample collection, and diagnostic procedures. Collect, process, and document biological samples for research and diagnostic purposes while maintaining accurate medical and research records. Support animal welfare and regulatory compliance through health assessments, documentation, and adherence to established animal care protocols. Collaborate with veterinarians, researchers, and animal care staff to support research and teaching activities across multiple animal facilities. Preferred Qualifications Experience monitoring patients during anesthesia and recovery. Experience collecting biological samples for diagnostic or research purposes. Experience working with large or small animals preferably in a research setting. Experience maintaining electronic medical records, research records, or animal health documentation.   What We're Looking For The ideal candidate will: Demonstrate strong attention to detail and recordkeeping abilities. Be comfortable working with a variety of animal species in a research environment. Possess strong communication and collaboration skills when working with researchers, veterinarians, and animal care staff. Be able to balance multiple priorities while maintaining high standards of animal care and regulatory compliance. Be proficient with computer systems and electronic recordkeeping. Additional Information Standard work schedule is Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Occasional after-hours, weekend, or holiday work may be required to support animal care, research activities, and clinical need Travel between multiple animal housing facilities on campus may be required. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. About Laboratory Animal Resources Laboratory Animal Resources supports Iowa State University's research, teaching, and outreach mission by providing exceptional animal care, veterinary services, research support, and compliance oversight. The department partners with investigators across campus to ensure the humane care and use of animals while advancing innovative research and scientific discovery. Through a commitment to animal welfare, collaboration, and service excellence, Laboratory Animal Resources plays a vital role in supporting groundbreaking research that benefits both human and animal health. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 7601a Original Posting Date: August 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 10, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19859 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Metabolomics_R19759": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Metabolomics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Metabolomics Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Metabolomics Research Facility is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to support collaborative and independent research focused on metabolomics and small molecule analysis using advanced mass spectrometry technologies. This position will play a key role in developing and executing metabolomics workflows for a diverse portfolio of research projects involving biological, environmental, agricultural, pharmaceutical, and biomanufacturing applications. The successful candidate will operate, maintain, and provide training on a variety of analytical instrumentation, including a Thermo Scientific Orbitrap Astral Mass Spectrometer, LC-MS, and GC-MS platforms. The individual will collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and external researchers to design experiments, prepare samples, acquire and analyze data, and interpret complex metabolomics datasets. Research activities will include both targeted and non-targeted metabolite profiling of a wide range of sample types, including animal models, human cell lines and cohorts, plants, microbial systems, environmental samples, and other novel biological materials. The postdoctoral researcher will assist in the development and implementation of new analytical methods and provide scientific consultation to researchers utilizing facility resources. Additional responsibilities include coordinating metabolomics research projects, supporting the training of laboratory users, contributing to the preparation of scientific reports and publications, presenting research findings at professional conferences, and participating in ongoing professional development opportunities. The position offers an opportunity to work in a highly collaborative research environment while advancing expertise in mass spectrometry, metabolomics, and interdisciplinary scientific research. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Analytical Chemistry, Bioinformatics, or a related field. Experience working with mass spectrometry instrumentation, associated software platforms, and data analysis workflows. Research experience in non-targeted metabolomics, global metabolomics, lipidomics, or closely related fields, including experimental design, sample preparation, data acquisition, data analysis, and post-acquisition bioinformatic and/or statistical analysis. Experience analyzing high-resolution LC-MS/MS data generated using Thermo Scientific Orbitrap instrumentation or similar high-resolution mass spectrometry platforms. Preferred Qualifications:   Experience using Thermo Scientific software applications, including Xcalibur, Compound Discoverer, TraceFinder, and LipidSearch. Experience operating, maintaining, troubleshooting, and optimizing complex analytical instrumentation in a research laboratory. Experience processing, analyzing, and interpreting raw mass spectrometry data. Experience with multi-omics data integration, statistical analysis, and biological interpretation of complex datasets. Demonstrated ability to support collaborative research projects and communicate technical findings to diverse scientific audiences. Department/Program & College Description: The W.M. Keck Metabolomics Research Laboratory in Iowa State University's Office of Biotechnology provides state-of-the-art mass spectrometry-based metabolomics services and expertise to researchers at Iowa State University and collaborators worldwide. Department Unit/Website: W.M. Keck Metabolomics Research Lab | Iowa State University Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: September 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: August 28, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 28, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19759 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Carpenter---Temporary_R19566": {
      "title": "Carpenter - Temporary",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Carpenter - Temporary Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Four years of experience in the trade, including apprenticeship. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: We are seeking a skilled Carpenter to perform a wide variety of journey-level carpentry, construction, repair, and installation work in support of facility operations. This role is responsible for building, installing, maintaining, and repairing structural and finish components, including doors, windows, walls, flooring, cabinetry, furniture, and other facility assets. The successful candidate will fabricate custom wood and metal components, perform drywall and surface finishing work, install hardware and flooring systems, and complete renovations and repairs to ensure safe, functional, and attractive facilities. This position also supports office and space reconfigurations through the installation and modification of modular furniture systems, ergonomic workstations, and audiovisual equipment. Responsibilities include interpreting blueprints and work orders, estimating materials and labor, ordering supplies, and developing practical solutions for unique construction and repair needs. The Carpenter works both independently and collaboratively, maintains a strong commitment to safety and quality craftsmanship, and may assist with training and guiding less experienced employees. Through a combination of technical expertise, problem-solving, and customer service, this position helps create and maintain welcoming and efficient environments for building occupants. Required Minimum Qualifications: • Four years of experience in the trade, including apprenticeship. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: January 31, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: 5061a Original Posting Date: July 7, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19566 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Biobased-Chemicals-Platform-Chief-Technology-Officer_R19809": {
      "title": "Biobased Chemicals Platform Chief Technology Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Biobased Chemicals Platform Chief Technology Officer Appointment Type: Contract Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities The Chief Technology Officer (CTO) will lead efforts to identify and accelerate the development of new technologies and innovations with strong commercial potential in the biobased products platform and related areas. This person will also serve as a driver for developing interfaces between the University and industry in this area to facilitate technology development and supporting collaborations. The CTO will possess and/or develop a deep understanding of innovations being developed within universities and across industry in the biobased products platform space with commercial potential. The CTO will also work closely with BioConnect staff to vet and prioritize opportunities for commercial development in Iowa. The CTO and BioConnect partners will provide ongoing oversight of prioritized ventures. The CTO will: Understand the technologies/innovations being developed within the universities and scout for relevant innovations across Iowa. Serve as a focal point at Iowa State University for industry to partner with and collaborate with researchers in this area. Lead technical vetting and prioritizing of innovations as potential commercial opportunities. Provide ongoing technical product development guidance to prioritized ventures, ensuring that timely progress is made against commercial development milestones. Understand University resources and expertise that could be of value for any developing ventures in the biobased products platform and, with BioConnect staff, develop and manage processes through which these resources can be accessed. Serve as a member of the Biobased Product platform leadership team. Serve as a partner with the NSF RuralSTAMINA Engine on Biomanufacturing. In partnership with BioConnect staff, the CTO will: Develop and implement strategies for translating innovations in Biobased Product platform to commercial products. Vet and prioritize for ongoing Biobased Product platform support, technologies/innovations based on their combination of technical potential and commercial viability. Guide prioritized ventures towards commercial development. Build and maintain relationships among platform researchers at the universities and with industry partners and coordinate (as well as conceive) joint activities and projects. Serve as primary contacts into their assigned platform. ​ Required Minimum Qualifications Master's degree or equivalent industrial experience in a relevant scientific discipline with at least 10 years of experience developing bioscience technical innovations for commercial application. Demonstrated ability to create and work towards a technological vision. Excellent interpersonal skills and proven collaborative leader. Will be required to work and elicit cooperation across a diverse range of stakeholders. Results‐driven, creative, commercially oriented leader with demonstrated ability to set and manage priorities. Understanding of project management discipline, with demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: PhD or equivalent industrial experience in a relevant scientific discipline with at least 10 years of experience developing bioscience technical innovations for commercial application. Experience working in industry, particularly in a product development and/or entrepreneurial role. Experience in the biobased products area. About Iowa is adopting a more aggressive, formalized approach to organizing for economic development in the bioscience sector, focusing on four technology platforms: biobased products, precision and digital agriculture, vaccines and immunotherapeutics, and medical devices. To coordinate this effort, BioConnect Iowa was established within the state’s public-private economic development partnership. Success will require an evergreen pipeline of commercially-oriented innovations. Universities will play a vital role filling this pipeline, and this position at Iowa State University will be central to that effort, focusing specifically on the biobased products platform. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or toll-free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: October 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Contract Original Posting Date: August 27, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 10, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19809 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Storekeeper-II_R19843": {
      "title": "Storekeeper II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Storekeeper II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • One year of work experience in storekeeping, accounting, business administration or job related work, or Any combination of such experience and post high school education that totals one year. • Possession of appropriate drivers license as required. Job Description: Keep ISU Dining moving from the warehouse to the table! As a Storekeeper II , you’ll play a key role in receiving, storing, inventorying, and delivering food, supplies, equipment, and other materials across ISU Dining locations. You’ll operate delivery vehicles and pallet jacks, load and unload materials, verify deliveries, complete transfer documentation, distribute products, and coordinate with delivery-site staff to ensure items are safely and accurately placed. You’ll also move furniture and equipment between Dining locations and serve as a resource for delivery logistics .     You’ll maintain inventory across coolers, freezers, and dry storage areas, ensuring proper stock rotation, receiving temperatures, product quality, and accurate records. You’ll fulfill orders and requisitions, conduct inventory counts, use tablet and inventory systems, complete Quality Assurance logs, and maintain clean, safe, and organized storage areas. The role also includes supporting and training student staff, assisting with equipment maintenance, coordinating vendor returns, and obtaining and maintaining ServSafe and forklift certifications. Some items may weigh up to 100 pounds.     Preferred Qualifications Experience in food service, warehouse, storeroom, receiving, or distribution operations.   Experience receiving, storing, rotating, and issuing food, supplies, or inventory.   Experience operating forklifts, pallet jacks, or other material-handling equipment.   Experience using computerized inventory, purchasing , or warehouse management systems.   Knowledge of food safety, sanitation, quality assurance, temperature monitoring, and FIFO inventory practices.     About the Department ISU Dining’s Foodstores Logistics team keeps dining operations running smoothly by receiving, storing, managing, and distributing the food, supplies, and equipment needed across campus dining locations. The team plays an essential behind-the-scenes role in ensuring products are available, properly handled, and delivered safely and efficiently to support the Cyclone dining experience.     Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program   If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 06 Original Posting Date: August 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 9, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19843 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
