    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Budget-and-Finance-Specialist-III_R19812": {
      "title": "Budget and Finance Specialist III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Budget and Finance Specialist III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Summary The Iowa State University Budget Office seeks qualified candidates for a Budget and Finance Specialist III position supporting the President’s Division. The Budget Office provides financial planning, analysis, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting services that support sound financial stewardship and informed decision-making across the university. This position serves as a strategic financial partner to divisional and senior leadership, providing leadership and direction for budget development, financial planning, forecasting, and resource management activities. The position works across multiple university units and funds to develop meaningful financial insights, identify risks and opportunities, and support decisions that advance Iowa State University’s mission and strategic priorities. Some key responsibilities for this role include the following: Providing strategic financial analysis and recommendations to leadership. Providing leadership and direction for budget development and financial planning. Developing multi-fund, multi-year forecasting and budget projections. Conducting financial analysis, scenario modeling, and data analytics. Identifying financial risks, opportunities, and potential efficiencies. Ensuring responsible use of resources and compliance with financial policies. Supporting effective use of Workday Finance and Planning systems and related processes. Providing financial guidance and training to divisional fiscal staff. Serving as the financial representative for the President’s Division on central finance committees and teams. Providing leadership and coordination across divisional fiscal operations. Serving as backup for institutional financial planning, analysis, and reporting. The ideal candidate should possess strong analytical, critical-thinking, time-management, and organizational skills, along with the ability to excel in a complex and dynamic environment. Effective verbal and written communication skills are essential. Additionally, the successful candidate will demonstrate sound professional judgment, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to translate complex financial information into clear, actionable insights. The candidate should thrive in a collaborative setting and demonstrate a commitment to service, integrity, ethical conduct, and continuous improvement. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing financial analysis, planning, recommendations, and business partner support to senior or executive leadership. Experience executing financial forecasting, budget development, and multi-year financial planning. Experience developing and executing financial analytics, modeling, and using data to inform business and resource decisions. Experience operating within enterprise financial planning, budgeting, or reporting systems and processes. Experience implementing AI or automation related to financial planning, analysis, reporting, or process improvement is a plus. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: August 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 8, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19812 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Departmental-Partner_R19385": {
      "title": "Departmental Partner - Business Administrator II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Departmental Partner - Business Administrator II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The College of Design seeks a qualified Departmental Partner (Business Administrator II) to oversee the business affairs and operations of assigned departments. The Departmental Partner plays a pivotal role within the Administrative Services Office (ASO) of the College of Design. This position provides a unique opportunity to apply a diverse set of skills and significantly influence the operation of our departments. The ASO values the unique contributions of each team member and encourages an atmosphere that nurtures growth and professional development.   This role reports to the college's Fiscal Officer and collaborates closely with chairs, faculty, and students. It involves a range of administrative duties crucial to the success of our academic efforts. It requires an adaptable, collaborative, and communicative individual proficient in multitasking.   Examples of Duties: Budget and Cost Center Management Manage the departmental cost center efficiently.  Approve financial transactions on Workday. Develop and prepare expense budgets and financial reports using workday for general appropriations (state funds), course fees (student fee funds) and foundation funds (outside college contributions). Analyze data to provide advice on complex budget issues, supporting informed financial decisions for the chairs. Exercise judgment in approving/denying expenditures, budget changes, and financial transactions. Review past course expenditures to advise faculty and chairs on appropriate course fees.  Provide compensation and non-compensation planning assistance to the chair. Approve expense reports for field trips and reconcile course fee worktags, deciding which account to use for expenses.  Manage budgets to ensure compliance with university policies and procedures.  Administrative and Departmental Support Coordinate course scheduling in collaboration with department chairs and manage associated logistics, including room scheduling; enter course/instructor in Workday Student. Attend departmental and college meetings, offering informed judgements to guide appropriate actions.  Accurately record meeting minutes and follow up on critical issues unless directed otherwise by the Chair.  Act as a reliable point of contact for chairs, managing their calendars and screening and responding to their calls when necessary. Facilitate departmental voting procedures on curriculum and other important matters.  Faculty and Student Support Serve as a trustworthy source of information and advice concerning department and college guidelines and policies for students and faculty. Support the faculty P&T process in partnership with the Chair, managing relevant documentation and coordinating with the Dean’s Assistant when necessary.  Hiring Process Support Oversee the graduate student hiring process, handling necessary paperwork, processing scholarships throughout the RA and TA hiring. Provide administrative assistance to faculty search committees, including room bookings, candidate travel arrangements, and job postings.   Support student employment processes. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Experience with financial management, including monthly account reconciliations, budget monitoring, and financial reporting. Proven ability to communicate and interpret policies, procedures, and financial information for faculty and other stakeholders to facilitate decision-making. Experience working within a higher education institution and knowledge of university business practices. Experience supporting academic department operations, including personnel administration, student employment and assistantships, course management in Workday, scholarship administration, and faculty support. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: June 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 7, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19385 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-or-Clinical-Track---Assistant---Associate---Full-Professor---Small-Animal-Surgery_R19845": {
      "title": "Tenure Track or Clinical Track - Assistant - Associate - Full Professor | Small Animal Surgery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track or Clinical Track - Assistant - Associate - Full Professor | Small Animal Surgery Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University invites applications for a full-time faculty position in the small animal surgery section of the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). We are in search of a small animal surgeon who is passionate about advancing the art of veterinary surgery and providing the highest level of care available to a large patient population coming from all corners of the Midwest. With a growing, vibrant, and cohesive group of faculty members in specialties including cardiology, dentistry, dermatology, emergency and critical care, radiology, internal medicine, ophthalmology, as well as medical and radiation oncology, the LVMC offers an incredible environment for collaboration, cross pollination, and innovative care and treatment of patients. This is bolstered by strong leadership in both the Department and the LVMC with administrators who continue to practice in clinics and truly embodies the spirit of the servant leader. Unlike many traditional academic positions, the opportunities at ISU are boundless in many respects. Though the clinical service is divided between soft tissue and orthopedic surgery, the percentage of clinic time spent on each service can be tailored to an individual's interest and desired career development. An opportunity for an endowed professorship in small animal surgery is available for a qualifying individual (e.g., Associate or Full Professor). The Small Animal Hospital at the LVMC is fully equipped with five state-of-the-art and spacious surgical suites complemented by top-of-the-line equipment to facilitate minimally invasive surgery (orthopedics and soft tissue) with near infrared technology, joint replacements, and interventional radiology procedures. With generous support from donors and the College administration, continued upgrades and addition of equipment is always available, including the recent purchase of a mobile radiology unit allowing for imaging in the operating suites to improve efficiency and further minimize surgical site contamination. The Department has also been proactive in encouraging and providing resources to support clinical research. A core laboratory has been established by the Department and is staffed by two staff researchers to aid clinical investigators with their projects. Internal funding is available to support clinical or preliminary research in preparation for outside grant application. Both primary investigator and collaborative research opportunities are available within the department and across the other College departments. We look forward to the application from candidates dedicated to exceptional patient care and with a strong desire to share their knowledge and clinical expertise to educate students, house officers, and technicians. The Department has placed heavy emphasis and efforts in providing personalized mentorship to ensure faculty success in both clinical and tenure-track positions with the understanding of the different but equally important roles. For those looking for a strongly collaborative environment to work in where peers from different specialties work together to provide the best treatment and patient care, we are confident that you will find no position more welcoming and supported than this one at ISU. Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree Successful completion of an American College of Veterinary Surgeons (ACVS), or European College of Veterinary Surgeons (ECVS) approved residency training program. Candidates in their third year of an approved surgical residency training program will also be considered an are encouraged to apply. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before the first day of employment Preferred Qualifications: Board certification in the American or European College of Veterinary Surgeons Additional years of active experience in small animal surgery An advanced degree (MS, PhD or equivalent) or notable potential for scholarship through both manuscript publication, granting activity or national scholarly, clinical, or education presentations, commensurate with their stage of career Documented commitment to veterinary instruction and education of students and/or house officers Department/Program & College Description: The LVMC is a state-of-the-art facility to designed to provide specialized care of comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients. As the nation's first public veterinary school, Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine takes pride in its heritage while shaping the future of veterinary professional practice, education, research and service. Ames, Iowa is a progressive community of 60,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines, and was recently voted as one of the best college towns in the nation. Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vcs / This position is open to some candidates eligible for employment-based immigration sponsorship. ISU is unable to provide H-1B immigration sponsorship for candidates who did not hold H-1B status as of September 20, 2025. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three (3) external to Iowa State references For full consideration, please apply on or before September 24, 2026 . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 25, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19845 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Nashua-IA/Agricultural-Specialist-II_R19819": {
      "title": "Agricultural Specialist II - Northeast Research Farm",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Agricultural Specialist II - Northeast Research Farm Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Iowa State University’s Northeast Research Farm in Nashua, Iowa, is seeking an Agricultural Specialist II to support agronomic research and farm operations. This hands-on position will operate and maintain tractors and other farm machinery, support field research activities, troubleshoot agricultural systems, and help maintain farm facilities and infrastructure. The successful candidate will work closely with faculty, researchers, staff, students, and external partners to support safe and efficient research farm operations. Experience operating and maintaining agricultural equipment is essential; experience with agronomic research or research plots is also beneficial. This is an excellent opportunity for an agricultural professional who enjoys hands-on equipment work, problem-solving, field operations, and supporting agricultural research. What You’ll Do Operate, maintain, troubleshoot, repair, and modify agricultural and research equipment, including tractors, tillage, planting, spraying, fertilization, and harvest equipment. Diagnose and address mechanical, hydraulic, electrical, electronic, GPS, and other equipment and farm system issues; coordinate repairs with vendors and service providers as needed. Support agronomic research projects by operating equipment and performing field activities including planting, spraying, soil sampling, crop scouting, harvesting, and data collection. Coordinate maintenance of farm facilities and infrastructure, including drainage systems, wetlands, bioreactors, buildings, water systems, and grounds. Maintain accurate equipment, farm operation, and research records and support research data collection and quality assurance. Provide technical guidance to staff, students, faculty, and equipment users involved in research and farm operations. Support field days, educational programs, stakeholder events, and Northeast Research Farm association activities. Coordinate scheduling, setup, and routine upkeep of the Borlaug Learning Center. Transport harvested grain to local elevators and perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Why Join Us At Iowa State University, you’ll have the opportunity to apply your agricultural and equipment expertise to research that directly benefits Iowa farmers and producers. The Northeast Research Farm conducts applied research that helps inform decisions about products, practices, application timing, and crop management. This position combines equipment operation and maintenance with field research and problem-solving, providing an opportunity to contribute to projects with practical applications across Iowa. You’ll collaborate with faculty, researchers, students, producers, and industry partners to generate and share information that advances agricultural practices. We’re looking for someone with strong agricultural knowledge, practical problem-solving skills, and an interest in applying their expertise to research that makes a difference. Learn more about the Northeast Research and Demonstration Farm , its research programs, facilities, and impact on Iowa agriculture. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s in Agriculture or related field Experience with farm research work or agronomic research plots Experience operating, repairing, and maintaining farm machinery used to conduct research on field plots Experience collecting, recording, and summarizing research data Experience observing, diagnosing, and providing remedies to crops Pesticide Applicator’s Certification Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This posting will remain Open Until Filled. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: August 25, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19819 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Public-Safety-Dispatcher-I_R19853": {
      "title": "Public Safety Dispatcher I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Public Safety Dispatcher I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Any combination of clerical education or experience and/or college or university level course work which is equivalent to two years of full-time employment. Job Description: The Department of Public Safety at Iowa State University is seeking candidates for a Public Safety Dispatcher I. Under general supervision, this position provides communications of a public safety nature for university police and other departments as well as surrounding law enforcement agencies and emergency response agencies utilizing multi-frequency radio, computer systems, telephone, TDD (telecommunications device for the deaf), and personal contact. In addition, this position is responsible for monitoring university emergency phones and multiple alarm systems. Preferred Qualifications Public Safety experience Dispatch experience The duties of this position require: Ability to perform multiple tasks at one time and to remain calm in stressful situations. Ability to enter and retrieve data from a computer terminal, PC or other keyboard device with speed and accuracy. Ability to communicate effectively and coherently over law enforcement radio channels while initiating and responding to radio communications. Skill in using equipment such as multi-frequency radio, teletype, telephone, TDD and computers. Skill in communicating with members of the public and departmental staff both orally and in writing. During training, this position will rotate through all shifts. At the conclusion of training, the employee will be assigned to a specific shift. Days off will be determined by shift assignment. Dispatchers are expected to work extra hours whenever large events are held on campus. This includes home football games, political events, Iowa Games, etc. Dispatchers are also expected to report to work during times of major disturbances or disasters on campus. Other Requirements: Must achieve certification in IOWA/NCIC (National Crime Information Center) System within 6 months of employment. Must attend 40-hour training course at Iowa Law Enforcement Academy within one year of employment. Must pass departmental background check. Iowa State University Police Department employees will support the Department’s vision and mission by operating in a fair, unbiased manner, which respects the rights and dignity of all individuals. Department employees’ everyday actions are guided by the Department’s values of Respect, Integrity, Caring, Honor, Excellence and Service (RICHES) and be grounded in the highest ethical and professional standards. Department employees are expected to work in partnership with the campus and area communities to provide leadership in solving community problems, preventing crime and providing a safe environment to fulfill the mission of the University. Employees will strive for excellence in fulfilling the Department’s Mission and Vision Statements, values and goals. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Operates a multi-frequency radio system in accordance with FCC regulations and completes a radio log and other records as required. • Operates a multi-line telephone system providing emergency and business information. • May be responsible for monitoring 911 phone system. • Monitors radio traffic from surrounding local and state law enforcement agencies and relays information to patrol units. • Dispatches duty personnel to requests for assistance or complaints. • Receives and provides information to visitors, faculty, staff, and students. • Notifies on-call personnel as required by departmental policy. • Receives and relays emergency weather and road information to public safety officers and to other university departments and the university administration as required. • Provides information to institutional public information services or outside news services on incidents and accident information as required. • Monitors, updates, and relays information regarding building alarms. • Operates a computer for the state crime computer network. • Maintains voice communication tapes and applicable files and manuals for reference at public safety dispatch office. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the geography of the university campus. • Knowledge of FCC regulations and public safety dispatching procedures. • Skill in using equipment such as multi-frequency radio, teletype, telephone, TDD, and computers. • Skill in communicating with members of the public and departmental staff both orally and in writing. • Ability to enter and retrieve data from a computer terminal, PC, or other keyboard device. • Ability to communicate effectively and coherently over law enforcement radio channels while initiating and responding to radio communications. • Ability to perform multiple tasks at one time and to remain calm in stressful situations. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 7591a Original Posting Date: August 24, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19853 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Substance-Use-and-Behavioral-Health-Specialist_R19709": {
      "title": "Substance Use and Behavioral Health Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Substance Use and Behavioral Health Specialist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 3 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you passionate about creating a holistic student experience that supports mental, physical, and emotional wellbeing? Are you interested in an opportunity where you get to engage with students and help them reach their full potential—academically and beyond? If so, Student Wellness with the Division of Student Affairs at Iowa State University is currently seeking applicants for a Substance Use and Behavioral Health Specialist! This individual plays a key role in advancing student health and wellbeing through strategic communication, data-informed storytelling, and health promotion initiatives. This position will be hired as a Wellness Program Specialist II. This position will focus on alcohol, substance use, and process/behavioral addiction prevention, recovery, and education.  What You’ll Do: Develop and deliver substance use prevention, recovery, and harm reduction programs for students. Coordinate and support the Collegiate Recovery Program, including student outreach, recovery coaching, and community-building initiatives. Plan, implement, and evaluate health promotion and educational programs related to alcohol, substance use, and behavioral addictions. Facilitate BASICS and CASICS interventions for self-referred students. Collaborate with campus and community partners to advance prevention, recovery, and wellness initiatives. Lead campus-wide substance use prevention and recovery projects and training programs. Coordinate naloxone education, distribution, and evaluation efforts. Develop and deliver presentations, workshops, and educational content for students, faculty, and staff. Collect, analyze, and report program data to support compliance, assessment, and continuous improvement efforts. Collaborate on marketing and communication strategies that promote wellness and recovery resources. Support broader Student Wellness initiatives, including mental health, violence prevention, basic needs, and other public health initiatives. Ensure compliance with university policies and applicable confidentiality, privacy, and risk management requirements. Occasional weekend/evening hours will be involved in this role. Preferred Qualifications: Specialized training or coursework in substance use prevention or recovery support (i.e. Alcohol, substances and/or behavioral addictions). Training or certification in Recovery Coaching, Certified Prevention Specialist (CPS), or similar prevention credential. Experience facilitating workshops, presentations and health promotion training. Experience applying motivational interviewing techniques. Experience using tools such as Smartsheet and/or Qualtrics. Department Description: Student Wellness at Iowa State University provides leadership in university strategy for health promotion and provides support programs aimed at creating a campus culture of wellbeing so that all students can thrive. Student Wellness plans, implements, and evaluates health education and prevention strategies that focus on health and wellness issues that directly affect student success, higher learning, and personal development such as: violence prevention, suicide, mental health, substance use, and more. To learn more, please visit Student Wellness . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before August 17th, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: August 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19709 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Police-Officer_R19850": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Police Officer Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Eligible to enroll in the Iowa Law Enforcement Academy and eligible to complete Board of Regents Field Training, OR • Possession of certification from the Iowa Law Enforcement Academy as a Law Enforcement Officer and eligible to complete Board of Regents Field Training, OR • Possession of law enforcement certification in another state and successful completion of all application and examination requirements as outlined in Iowa Administrative Code 501-3.8(80B) and eligible to complete Board of Regents Field Training Job Description: The Department of Public Safety at Iowa State University is seeking candidates for Non-certified and Certified officers to join our team. This is a 24 hour operation, 365 days a year. Officers will be expected to work holidays that fall within their regular work schedule as well as during home football games and other major events that occur on campus. Expected to report for duty when major natural disasters or other emergency situation affecting the campus occur. Permanent, 12 Months, Full Time, 40 hours/week, Rotating Schedule, Shift assignment to be determined after completion of training program. During training will rotate through all shifts. Days off are also on a rotating schedule. In accordance with the general requirements for law enforcement officers under Iowa Admin. Code 501-2.1, the applicant selected for this position, both uncertified and certified, must be a U.S. citizen. Must have and maintain a valid U.S. state driver’s license and the ability to be authorized to drive University vehicles. Non-Certified: This is an entry level police officer position. The officer will attend and must successfully complete the Iowa Law Enforcement Basic Level I or Level II Academy to become certified as a peace officer in the state of Iowa. Upon successful completion of the academy, the officer will return to the ISU campus and be placed under the direct supervision of a police training officer. During this period, the officer will perform all the duties of a law enforcement officer, including patrolling the university campus and outlying areas; enforcing local, state, and federal laws as well as campus rules and regulations; responding to calls for service; initiating police reports; performing follow-up investigations as needed; directing traffic, and other duties as assigned. During basic training, will attend the Iowa Law Enforcement Academy M-F. During field training, will rotate through all shifts with varying hours and days off. Actual shift assignment will follow completion of all required training. All qualified applicants will be invited to take a written test and physical test the week of September 21st, 2026 . More details about the testing and testing dates will be provided later. Non-certified applications will be accepted through September 10th, 2026 to allow for testing to take place on the above date. Applicants successfully hired who are non-certified will be eligible for recruitment incentive payments* in the total amount of $3,500.  *Full details and terms of payment will be provided in payment agreements for those successfully hired. Certified: The officer is placed under the direct supervision of a police training officer. During this period, the officer will perform all the duties of a law enforcement officer including patrolling the university campus and outlying areas; enforcing local, state, and federal laws as well as campus rules and regulations; responding to calls for service; initiating police reports, performing follow-up investigations as needed; directing traffic, and other duties as assigned. Out of state certified applicants will be required to pass a physical test and written test to be considered for the position. Qualified in-state candidates will be individually scheduled for interviews. Applicants successfully hired who are certified law enforcement officers will be eligible for recruitment incentive payments* in the total amount of $10,000. *Full details and terms of payment will be provided in payment agreements for those successfully hired. The department is accepting applications until the positions are filled, and the vacancies may close without notice.  Iowa State University Police Department employees will support the Department’s vision and mission by operating in a fair, unbiased manner, which respects the rights and dignity of all individuals. Department employees’ everyday actions are guided by the Department’s values of Respect, Integrity, Caring, Honor, Excellence and Service (RICHES) and be grounded in the highest ethical and professional standards. Department employees are expected to work in partnership with the campus and area communities to provide leadership in solving community problems, preventing crime and providing a safe environment to fulfill the mission of the University. Employees will strive for excellence in fulfilling the Department’s Mission and Vision Statements, values and goals. In addition to Iowa State University's standard background check, candidates are required to successfully complete additional background checks, thorough reference checks, and pre-employment health evaluation(s) in accordance with the Department of Public Safety's hiring practices. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Patrols assigned zone by motor vehicle, bicycle, or on foot to prevent, discover, and deter the commission of crime; to enforce criminal and traffic laws and university rules and regulations; and to check the security of buildings, functioning of outdoor lighting and traffic signals, and road conditions. Monitors and directs vehicular and pedestrian traffic as required. • Responds to radio dispatched calls for a variety of services including investigation of alarms, animal control, assistance to motorists, building maintenance problems, domestic problems, thefts, and other acts against persons or property. • Investigates, reports, and records traffic violations and accidents by interviewing witnesses, measuring distances, sketching diagrams, taking photographs, and conducting field sobriety tests to determine cause and fault. • Investigates harm, damage or threats of potential harm or damage to persons or property by interviewing witnesses and conducting visual or audio surveillance or searches; detects and collects evidence; travels to other jurisdictions to investigate crimes that occurred on university property as necessary. • Arrests violators or suspects by using minimum force. Processes arrested persons by taking photographs, obtaining fingerprints, and writing arrest reports; transports violators to jail. • Determines appropriate action to be taken by weighing evidence and applying knowledge of law to solve the problem and administer justice; prepares and processes documents such as citations, complaints, affidavits, and warrants. • Records information at scene of crime or accident by sketching diagrams, taking photographs, or taking notes. Prepares reports for use by department, university or social service agency, in court testimony or for insurance claims. • Testifies in court or by deposition to present information accumulated at scene and to give professional opinions for criminal justice and insurance purposes. • Performs rescue functions at accidents, emergencies and disasters to include directing traffic for long periods of time, administering first responder level service at the medical model level; lifting, dragging, and carrying people away from dangerous situations; and securing buildings and evacuating occupants. • Responds to fire and ambulance calls to direct traffic, escort fire and ambulance vehicles, and prevent crime. • Inspects and maintains law enforcement equipment by observing and cleaning to keep the equipment in reliable operating condition. • Transfers deposits between the university and banks by personal pick up and delivery to maintain security of funds. • Determines content for various public safety programs such as crime prevention, personal safety, playground safety, bike safety, and provides delivery to the university or community. • Assists other agencies in serving warrants by delivering and serving in person for timely disposition of cases, and any other assigned duties. • Provides advice and general information to students, staff, and campus visitors. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of state criminal and traffic code and city ordinances; and university and departmental policy and operating procedures. • Knowledge of patrol, investigative, and arrest procedures. • Knowledge of the location of buildings and facilities, including fire and environmental emergency panels of the university and city. • Knowledge of location and services of various university departments and community agencies. • Knowledge of legal documents and processing procedures. • Skill in oral communications as demonstrated by effective ability to provide general information and directions, mediate disputes, interview witnesses and suspects, testify as a witness in court, and make program presentations. • Skill in written communications to produce reports and documents in the English language with clearly organized thoughts using proper sentence structure, format, punctuation, and grammar. • Skill in administering first aid and cardiopulmonary resuscitation. • Skill in reconstructing accidents from interviews and physical evidence. • Skill in operating vehicles both day and night in emergency situations involving speeds in excess of posted limits, in congested traffic, and in unsafe conditions due to such factors as fog, smoke, rain, ice, and snow. • Skill in operating radios and other law enforcement equipment. • Skill in analyzing situations and using judgment to make appropriate decisions. • Ability to communicate effectively and coherently over law enforcement radio channels while initiating and responding to radio communications. • Ability to patrol on foot or bicycle; remain in standing or sitting position for long periods of time; pursue fleeing suspects; and perform rescue operations which may involve entering and exiting vehicles quickly, lifting, carrying or dragging heavy objects, climbing over and pulling oneself over obstacles, jumping down from elevated surfaces, climbing through openings, jumping over obstacles, ditches and streams, crawling in confined areas, balancing on uneven or narrow surfaces, and using bodily force to gain entrance through barriers. • Ability to use sufficient physical force in apprehension of law violators. • Ability to work and remain calm in stressful situations. • Ability to work outside in extreme weather conditions. • Ability to hear and see acutely during day and night time conditions. • Ability to enter and retrieve data from a computer terminal, personal computer, or other keyboard device.   Probationary Period: To allow for the necessary time to complete the academy, on-campus training, and assessment as a certified police officer, the probationary period for a Police Officer will be 18 months. If a Police Officer has completed the academy prior to appointment, the probationary period will be 12 months. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: DPS18 Original Posting Date: August 24, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 10, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19850 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Associate-Professor-of-Practice_R19836": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Associate Professor of Practice Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Urban Planning and Development at Iowa State University invites applications for the position of Associate Professor of Practice to teach community-focused undergraduate and graduate studio courses. The initial appointment for this position will be one semester with a start date of January 1, 2027, and ending on May 15, 2027. Additional teaching opportunities may be available based on departmental needs and the candidate's interests. This is a part-time position. Planning studios are professional experiences in the curriculum. Working in partnership with external clients, students function as a professional planning consulting team to address real-world planning topics. The instructor guides students through all phases of the planning process, including project design, applied research, stakeholder engagement, data collection and analysis, development of planning recommendations, and preparation of professional planning products. The studios emphasize experiential learning, collaboration, project management, professional ethics, and client communication. The candidate will be expected to contribute meaningfully to the department's teaching mission. We are looking for individuals with strong communication skills who share our commitment to fostering excellence. Additional expectations are: Develop and oversee a client-based planning project in collaboration with a community partner. Mentor students through applied planning research, community engagement, plan development, and professional presentations. Supervise student project teams and foster a collaborative studio environment. Coordinate meetings, field visits, and communication with community partners and stakeholders. Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback on individual and team work. Produce a high-quality professional planning product that meets client expectations and supports student learning outcomes. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in urban planning, or a closely related field. 10 or more years of professional planning experience in public, private, or nonprofit practice. Preferred Qualifications: AICP certification Demonstrated knowledge of planning processes, public engagement, and project management. Expertise in one or more planning practice areas such as comprehensive planning, housing, economic development, sustainability, resilience, transportation, land use, or community development. Experience working with interdisciplinary teams and community partners. Department/Program & College Description: About the Department of Urban Planning and Development The Department of Urban Planning and Development is one of only 16 accredited undergraduate planning programs in the United States, and we have an outstanding faculty who are committed to excellence in the teaching of planning at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Through the department's degree programs, students develop the skills and experience to become practicing planning professionals. Some of the major areas of expertise include: land-use planning and zoning environmental planning transportation planning site planning urban design In addition, our students regularly work with communities in Iowa to understand the issues and challenges and how planners play a role in addressing them. We also undertake high-quality research on behalf of federal and state government, business, the nonprofit sector, and other funding agencies, all of which feed into the courses we teach to give our students a well-rounded foundation for their future careers. Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department's design program, see https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/upd/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by October 1, 2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at http://jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R19836. The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: 1) Letter of application that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications. 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Contact information for three references, including name, their position, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information Direct questions to Biswa Das, Chair, Department of Urban Planning and Development, at bdas@iastate.edu. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 24, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19836 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Early-Childhood-Teacher-Assistant_R19686": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Teacher Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Early Childhood Teacher Assistant Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Job Description: The Child Development Laboratory School in the Department of Human Development and Family Studies is seeking an Assistant Early Childhood Teacher. The Assistant Early Childhood Teacher fosters a safe, engaging, and inclusive learning environment, communicates with families as needed, and works with the classroom teachers and other program staff to support high-quality early childhood education. Collaborates with faculty, staff, and students within the Department of Human Development and Family Studies and across Iowa State University to support research, teaching, student learning, and interdisciplinary initiatives. The Child Development Laboratory School is accredited by the National Association for the Education of Young Children (NAEYC), licensed by the Iowa Department of Health and Human Services, and maintains a 5-Star rating through Iowa Quality for Kids (IQ4K). The program also serves as a teaching and learning laboratory for students in the Early Childhood Education Program. Example of Duties Collaborates with the teachers in the room to supervise the classroom. Serves as a role model for best practice in the classroom. Observe, document, and communicate children's behavioral and developmental needs while collaborating with families and colleagues. Maintains a safe classroom through adherence to HHS, NAEYC, IQ4K, CACFP, Caring for Our Children, and other safety standards recognized by the field of early childhood. Maintains adherence to state “teacher to child” ratios for their age group. Engages with parents’ daily, initiating written and/or face-to-face communication taking into consideration the communication needs of those with varied cultural and ethnic backgrounds. Assists in partnerships with departments on campus to encourage non HDFS student use of the Lab School. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with children from birth through age five in group early childhood settings, including supporting children with special needs. Demonstrated knowledge of developmentally appropriate practices and early childhood development. Experience planning, implementing, and assessing developmentally appropriate curriculum and learning experiences. Strong collaboration and teamwork skills, with the ability to work effectively with children, families, and colleagues. State of Iowa teaching license (initial, standard, or master) in Early Childhood Education or Early Childhood Special Education or Elementary Education with an Early Childhood Education Endorsement (endorsement 100, 1001, 262 and/or 103). Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS804 Original Posting Date: August 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19686 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Term-Faculty-of-Teaching-or-Practice-for-the-Department-of-Finance_R19832": {
      "title": "Term Faculty of Teaching or Practice for the Department of Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Term Faculty of Teaching or Practice for the Department of Finance Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Finance in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University is now accepting applications for a full-time term (i.e., non-tenure track) faculty position at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor, or Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Practice. This position will teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels in Finance beginning Spring semester, January 2027. Anticipated course load is four courses per semester (i.e., a 4-4 teaching load). This position will consist primarily of in-person classroom instruction on the Ames, IA campus, with the possibility of some online course delivery. The successful candidate will additionally contribute to departmental service and/or student activities (such as case competition preparation, etc., depending on course load assignment). The initial term length will be for one year, ending December 31, 2027, with the possibility for renewal.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Business or closely related field Qualified candidates must meet the college’s standards to be qualified under AACSB accreditation standards Preferred Qualifications: Prior collegiate teaching experience of at least five years in finance or closely related field Professional industry experience (e.g., financial services, corporate finance) Professional credentials in finance (e.g., CFA) PhD in Finance or closely related field Solid technological skills to support use of online instructional tools Department/Program & College Description: The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement. With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/about-ivy/academic-d Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 31, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References To be fully considered for this position, please apply on or before October 14, 2026 . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position, please contact the Department Chair, Dr. Bidisha Chakrabarty at bidisha@iastate.edu. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 24, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19832 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer-in-Counseling-Psychology_R19827": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer in Counseling Psychology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Psychology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for a part-time, term faculty position at the rank of Lecturer to teach a graduate course in group counseling in the department’s Counseling Psychology Ph.D. program. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching an in-person graduate-level course focused on the theory and practice of group counseling. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering course instruction, facilitating experiential learning activities, evaluating student learning, and providing students with feedback and guidance consistent with doctoral-level training in counseling psychology. The appointment is for the Spring 2027 semester, with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in counseling or clinical psychology by the start date of the appointment Training or professional experience in group counseling or group psychotherapy Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in counseling or clinical psychology Experience providing group counseling or psychotherapy Experience working with or training doctoral students in counseling psychology Evidence of effective teaching Current licensure as a psychologist Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Psychology at Iowa State University offers thriving Ph.D. programs in social, cognitive, and counseling psychology and is home to the largest number of undergraduate majors in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. Consistent with the university’s land-grant mission, our research builds psychological theory through empirical investigations and applies scientific findings to benefit individuals, communities, and society. Our department is highly collegial, supportive, and collaborative. The Counseling Psychology Ph.D. program prepares students for professional practice, research, and teaching in counseling psychology. Students receive broad training in psychological science and professional practice through coursework, research, supervised clinical experiences, and other professional development opportunities. Iowa State University is located in Ames, a vibrant community of approximately 66,000 in central Iowa, about 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living, and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of the state’s largest metropolitan area. More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective Department Unit/Website: https://psychology.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by October 1, 2026, but will be accepted until the position is filled . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19827 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Seed-Pathology_R19814": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Seed Pathology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Seed Pathology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology and the Seed Science Center in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Iowa State University invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the area of seed pathology. We seek candidates with broad expertise in seed pathology whose research will support the development of state-of-the-art diagnostic tools that facilitate the detection of seedborne pathogens with particular emphasis on viruses, bacteria, and fungi. Candidates whose expertise encompasses the use of high-throughput sequencing and associated computational pipelines are of particular interest. The position is 65% research, 30% teaching, and 5% service. The successful candidate is expected to develop an externally funded, high-impact research program that engages students in the broad areas of plant pathology, seed pathology and bioinformatics while also participating in service to the university. ISU has extensive shared facilities for biological research, including -omics technology for genetics, genomics and microbiome studies and high-performance computing. The collaborative environment is enhanced by interdisciplinary and disciplinary graduate majors that promote cross-fertilization within labs. The successful candidate will have an office and laboratory in the Seed Science Building, which houses the Seed Science Center. The Seed Science Center is a globally recognized hub of excellence in seed testing, research, education, systems, and international programs. It is a leader in developing science to inform policy to benefit the world seed trade. The Center is home to the Seed Lab, one of the largest public testing laboratories in the U.S. that has provided accurate and professional seed testing services to growers and the seed industry for more than 130 years. The Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology serves as home to the ISU Plant and Insect Diagnostic Clinic, has access to numerous field research facilities, and administers a vibrant and experiential undergraduate microbiology program. Faculty have strengths in extension, teaching, and the scholarship of teaching and learning, and research across the full spectrum from fundamental to applied.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Plath Pathology, Plant Science or a closely related field with experience in the broad area of seed pathology   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of strong potential for conducting innovative research in seed pathology that includes the development of diagnostic tests for pathogens Evidence for the use of high-throughput sequencing and associated computational pipelines Evidence of a strong publication record in internationally recognized journals Evidence of strong potential for research mentoring Evidence of strong potential for collaborative research Evidence of strong potential for securing extramural funding Evidence of strong potential for evidence-based, innovative teaching  Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on \"Apply\" and complete the Employment Application. The application should include: 1) Cover Letter describing the qualifications for the position (2 pages max) 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Research Statement detailing experience and future plans (3 pages max) 4) Teaching Statement detailing philosophy, experience, and future plans (2 pages max) 5) Names and contact information for three references For guaranteed consideration, applications should be received by January 4th, 2027. Questions regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Scott Heuchelin ( scott3@iastate.edu ), or the Chair of the Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology, Steven Harris ( stevenh1@iastate.edu ). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19814 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Manager-Human-Resources-Delivery_R19813": {
      "title": "Manager Human Resources Delivery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Manager Human Resources Delivery Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Iowa State University is seeking a  Manager, Human Resource Delivery  to lead a team within University Human Resources (UHR) that supports the College of Veterinary Medicine. This role serves as a strategic partner and trusted resource, advancing the university’s mission as a world-class institution through high-quality human capital solutions. The Manager leads a team of HR professionals, fostering a culture of service excellence and working alongside campus leadership to optimize UHR practices across the employee lifecycle. Key Responsibilities Leading and mentoring,  a team of HR Coordinators, promoting accountability, professional growth, and consistent, high‑quality service delivery.  Strategic Advisor,  providing guidance to client leadership on organizational and talent strategies. This includes identifying talent gaps, developing action plans to meet unit goals, and aligning local human capital strategies with institutional priorities. Employee Relations and Regulatory Compliance, o versee complex employee relations matters, including conducting investigations and advising on disciplinary actions. Ensure institutional compliance with federal, state, and local employment laws (such as FLSA) while partnering with offices like General Counsel and Equal Opportunity to mitigate risk. Operational Excellence and Process Improvement, s upport the optimization of HR systems by providing solution-focused feedback on business processes. Drive change management initiatives and standardize HR practices across service teams to enhance operational efficiency and the client experience. Compensation and Consultative Services:  Provide consultation on salary policies, performance management, and disability/leave referrals. This includes conducting pay equity analyses to ensure alignment with compensation structures and guiding managers through the employee performance review and improvement process.  Data-Driven Decision Making and Communication,  utilize HR analytics and workforce data to identify trends and inform leadership decision-making. Disseminate and explain HR communications regarding policy and strategy changes to ensure stakeholders are well-informed. This is an excellent opportunity for an HR professional who thrives in a collaborative environment, values strong partnerships, and is motivated by continuous improvement. The successful candidate will be energized by supporting academic and research excellence through thoughtful, strategic, and service‑focused human resources leadership. Preferred Qualifications: Supervisory and leadership experience with a proven track record of developing competencies in direct reports. Experience working with organizational leadership on human capital and HR strategy implementation. Proven ability to interpret, train, and communicate complex HR policies and principles. Professional certification such as PHR, SPHR, or an equivalent. For more information about Human Resources, please visit: University Human Resources Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by September 2, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS811 Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19813 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Statistics-1_R19800": {
      "title": "Two Assistant Professors in Statistics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Two Assistant Professors in Statistics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Statistics, at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, seeks two tenure-track assistant professors with expertise in statistics and data science beginning August 16, 2027. One of the positions will have a particular emphasis on sports analytics. The successful candidates will develop and sustain a high-quality and high-impact research program, successfully compete for external funding, and collaborate with world-class researchers at Iowa State in statistics and other disciplines.  Further, the successful candidates will engage in professional and institutional service, teach graduate and undergraduate students, and advise graduate students in one of the first and largest statistics graduate programs in the country. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent degree in statistics or closely related discipline by appointment start date Preferred Qualifications: Foundational training in statistics and data science Ability to teach statistics and data science classes at the undergraduate and graduate levels Ability to develop and sustain a high-impact research program with the potential to secure external research funding Ability to contribute to Iowa State University’s growing strength in data science Ability to contribute to Iowa State University's growing strength in data science and, for one position, sports analytics Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Statistics is jointly administered by the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences.  The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences is one of the world’s leading institutions of agriculture, with more than 160 years of leadership in science, education and extension. The college educates future leaders, conducts mission-oriented research, and shares new knowledge for the betterment of Iowa and the world. The college is one of eight colleges at Iowa State University, which is one of the most influential land grant universities in the nation.   Central to Iowa State University’s mission, the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) is a collaborative, vibrant community of faculty, students and staff, committed to learning, research, and innovation. With 21 departments, one professional school, 49 majors, and over 20 interdisciplinary programs, LAS faculty support student success and engage in pathbreaking research across a wide range of fields.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.stat.iastate.edu   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References 4) Additional documents submitted as one combined PDF:  Research Statement Teaching Statement For guaranteed consideration, please apply before October 1, 2026 .  Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. If you have questions regarding the position, please contact Kathy Kiesling (kiesling@iastate.edu). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 20, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19800 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Marketing---Sales-Management---Professional-Selling_R19085": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Marketing – Sales Management / Professional Selling",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Marketing – Sales Management / Professional Selling Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Marketing in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University is seeking a successful candidate at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. The primary research area is in Sales Management and/or Professional Selling. This position is a full-time (9-month) appointment starting 8/16/2027. An earlier start date in January 2027 will also be considered. This individual will be affiliated with the Ivy Sales Forum in a research capacity. Additional administrative involvement with the Ivy Sales Forum is an option, but not required, depending on the selected individual’s preferences. Initial review of applications will begin on August 10, 2026, but applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Ivy faculty members are committed to offering a high-quality education in a way that prepares students for their real-world experiences. We combine quality curriculum, internationally known faculty, and a welcoming atmosphere to create an unmatched business education, whether students are seeking degrees at the bachelor, master, or PhD level. Our internationally known faculty in the Debbie and Jerry Ivy College of Business are engaged in a wide variety of research. The topics are broad and aim to link theory and practice in an academically rigorous fashion. Our faculty focus on current and future issues encountered by industry and organizations at all levels. Issues involve both micro- and macro-related topics that affect internal business operations as well as society at large. The goal of our research is to deliver a steady flow of thought-provoking articles in premier journals. Position Responsibilities: The successful candidate will conduct high-impact scholarly research publishable in premier and high-quality marketing journals and will teach marketing-related courses at the undergraduate, Master's, and/or PhD levels. The candidate is expected to significantly grow and shape the department's research profile. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in marketing or a closely related field Must meet the college's standards to be Scholarly Academic Qualified under AACSB Accreditation standards A strong portfolio of research in sales management and/or professional selling, aimed at premier marketing journals (such as the Journal of Marketing Research, Journal of Marketing, and Journal of the Academy of Marketing Science) A record of effective teaching of marketing and/or sales courses Additionally, for Associate/Full rank: At least six years of experience as a full-time, tenure track or tenured faculty member, with an outstanding record of scholarship eligible for a tenured position at Iowa State University Preferred Qualifications: An advanced research pipeline, including papers invited for revision at premier journals Prior publications in premier marketing journals Experience in mentoring junior faculty and/or doctoral students Track record of collaborating with industry partners on research Department/Program & College Description: The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, conducts and shares research to educate tomorrow's business leaders so they are prepared to deal with multi-disciplinary, global challenges. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and PhD programs and is accredited by The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. The Ivy College is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards, and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college's mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow's business leaders. The Department of Marketing houses the Ivy Sales Forum, an academic center that strives to advance the growth and effectiveness of professional sales and works along with its corporate partners to provide the Professional Sales Certificate students with relevant experiential learning opportunities. The Forum is currently supported by nine Corporate Partners and eleven Corporate Members, each of which engages with sales students and sales faculty to support the teaching and research missions of the College ( https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/about-ivy/academic-departments/marketing/ivy-sales-forum/ ). The department also boasts a strong PhD program, with recent R1 placements, a behavioral lab for experimental research, research grant opportunities funded by the Ivy Sales Forum, and productive research faculty (#69 in marketing publications among North American schools since 2019 per the UTD Business School Research Rankings). Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/marketing/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For questions about this position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Andrew Crecelius at acrecli@iastate.edu. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before August 10, 2026 . This position will remain open until filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: May 1, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19085 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Police-Sergeant-Supervisory_R19784": {
      "title": "Police Sergeant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Police Sergeant Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Possession of certification from the Iowa Law Enforcement Academy as a Law Enforcement Officer, or • Possession of law enforcement certification in another state and successful completion of all application and examination requirements as outlined in Iowa Administrative Code 501-3.8(80B), and • Two years experience at the Police Officer or equivalent level; or AA/AAS in Criminal Justice or Police Science or 60 semester hours/90 quarter hours from an accredited college or university and one year experience at the Police Officer or equivalent level. Special Required Qualifications Valid U.S. Driver's License Job Description: The Department of Public Safety at Iowa State University is seeking a qualified candidate for the Police Sergeant role who will act as shift supervisor in the absence of the Lieutenant. This person will be responsible for: Assigning tasks Reviewing reports Overseeing the day-to-day operations of the shift Updating the shift Lieutenant regarding shift activities Providing input into employee evaluations Providing backup for other public safety staff at the scene of incidents and accidents as requested or required This position may also be subject to rotation through other Sergeant assignments. Under general supervision, exercises functional supervisory control over a unit of Police Officers and Trainees, Public Safety Officers, and Public Safety Dispatchers as directed to ensure proper performance of duties. Provides back-up for other Public Safety staff at the scene of accidents and incidents. Iowa State University Police Department employees will support the Department’s vision and mission by operating in a fair, unbiased manner, which respects the rights and dignity of all individuals. Department employees’ everyday actions are guided by the Department’s values of Respect, Integrity, Caring, Honor, Excellence and Service (RICHES) and be grounded in the highest ethical and professional standards. Department employees are expected to work in partnership with the campus and area communities to provide leadership in solving community problems, preventing crime and providing a safe environment to fulfill the mission of the University. Employees will strive for excellence in fulfilling the Department’s Mission and Vision Statements, values and goals. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a university law enforcement agency Applicants successfully hired who are certified law enforcement officers will be eligible for recruitment incentive payments* in the total amount of $10,000. *Full details and terms of payment will be provided in payment agreements for those successfully hired. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Monitors activities of subordinate staff by driving through their assigned zones on campus and by other means observing and reviewing their work. Reports violation of departmental policies to Lieutenant and recommends corrective action. •  Directs and instructs shift officers and advises subordinate staff on departmental policies. Provides the communication link from the Lieutenant and department administration to the Police Officers and back. •  Evaluates strengths and weaknesses of Police Officers for input into performance appraisals. •  Interviews, recommends hiring and supervises the training of new employees; checks and evaluates the performance of subordinate personnel, makes recommendations with respect to personnel actions. •  May assume duties of the shift commander in the absence of the Lieutenant. •  Performs the duties of Police Officer. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities •  Knowledge of state criminal and traffic code, city ordinances, and Constitutional law. •  Skill in observing and reviewing the work of Police Officers. • Knowledge, skills, and abilities required to perform the duties of Security Guard, Police Officer, and Public Safety Dispatcher. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 22 Original Posting Date: August 17, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19784 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Ames-National-Laboratory-Research-Technologist-II_R19788": {
      "title": "Ames National Laboratory Research Technologist II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Ames National Laboratory Research Technologist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 3 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Division of Critical Materials (DCM) at Ames National Laboratory is searching for a qualified laboratory technologist who will play a central role in enabling the efficient execution of research activities across the Division. This position will provide flexible, high-impact technical support to multiple research teams, ensuring continuity, quality, and productivity in both routine and specialized laboratory operations. The technologist will be responsible for maintaining and optimizing shared laboratory infrastructure, including preventive maintenance, calibration, troubleshooting, and coordination of repairs for key equipment and instrumentation. The position will also support Group Leaders and Principal Investigators (PIs) in the installation and commissioning of new equipment, as needs arise. This role will help ensure that facilities and tools remain fully operational and aligned with safety and performance requirements. A component of the position involves user support and training. The technologist will onboard new researchers, provide hands-on training in equipment use and laboratory protocols, and promote best practices. The position will coordinate with group leaders, researchers, technicians, and students in DCM and across Ames National Laboratory to ensure safe, efficient, and reproducible experimental work. The position will also contribute directly to experimental efforts as needed, such as supporting activities in materials synthesis, sample preparation, characterization, and data collection. This support will be adaptive, responding to evolving project needs and priorities across multiple programs. In addition, the technologist will collaborate closely with scientists, engineers, and other technical staff within the division and across Ames National Laboratory to coordinate shared resources, assist in cross-divisional projects, and facilitate communication. The ideal candidate is highly organized, technically proficient, and proactive, with the ability to operate effectively in a dynamic, multi-project research environment. Strong communication skills, attention to detail, and a commitment to safety and continuous improvement are essential. Preferred Qualifications: Degree in Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Physics, Chemistry, or a closely related field. Demonstrated experience maintaining, calibrating, and troubleshooting laboratory instrumentation in research or industrial environment. Hands-on experience supporting installation and commissioning of scientific or process equipment Experience developing and implementing standard operating procedures (SOPs) and training users on laboratory equipment and protocols Practical experience supporting experimental workflows, including materials synthesis, sample preparation, and/or materials characterization Working knowledge of laboratory safety practices and compliance requirements (e.g., chemical handling, high-temperature systems, inert atmospheres) Experience working in multidisciplinary team environments and supporting multiple projects or users concurrently Strong organizational skills with experience in data collection, documentation, and basic data analysis Experience managing laboratory supplies, inventory systems, and coordinating with vendors or service providers Hands-on experience in metals and alloys processing, including melt processing and/or powder metallurgy Familiarity with operation and maintenance of equipment such as furnaces, welding systems, melting units, milling equipment, sintering systems, glove boxes (inert environments), and powder handling/processing tools Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answer yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory! Ames National Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today including delivering critical materials solutions to the nation. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Department Unit/Website: www.ameslab.gov   Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory. Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: August 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19788 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Turfgrass-Research-Scientist_R19637": {
      "title": "Turfgrass Research Scientist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Turfgrass Research Scientist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: The Department of Horticulture in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Iowa State University is seeking a Turfgrass Research Scientist to help advance nationally recognized turfgrass program focused on athletic field safety, golf course management, sports turf performance, turfgrass adaptation, and sustainable management practices. This position offers a unique blend of outdoor field research, laboratory work, equipment operation, data analysis, and scientific collaboration. Working alongside faculty, students, and industry partners, you'll conduct research that improves the safety, performance, and management of athletic fields, golf courses, parks, and other managed turf systems. Whether your goal is to become a leader in the turfgrass industry or pursue graduate education, this position provides an exceptional opportunity to develop technical expertise, gain hands-on research experience, and explore innovative ideas in a collaborative environment where learning through experimentation is encouraged. Key Responsibilities Coordinate and execute applied turfgrass field research by preparing research sites, implementing experimental protocols, scheduling field activities, and overseeing student employees. Establish, maintain, and evaluate turfgrass research plots through mowing, irrigation management, fertilizer and pesticide applications, and cultivation practices. Collect, document, and manage research data, including plant and soil samples, turfgrass quality and color ratings, weed assessments, soil moisture measurements, and surface hardness and stability testing. Assist in developing and refining research methods and protocols, maintain research databases, perform data quality control, and conduct statistical analyses. Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and external partners to support research projects, scientific publications, grant proposals, field demonstrations, and extension and outreach activities. Present research findings at field days, scientific conferences, and industry meetings, prepare educational displays and demonstration plots, and provide tours of research facilities for visitors and stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Horticulture, Turfgrass Management, Agronomy, Plant Science, or a related field. Experience establishing, maintaining, and managing turfgrass research plots or production systems, including irrigation management. Experience operating, calibrating, troubleshooting, and maintaining turfgrass or agricultural equipment. Experience collecting, managing, and analyzing research data. Experience applying fertilizers, herbicides, fungicides, or other crop protection products in accordance with research protocols and applicable regulations. Experience presenting research findings, contributing to scientific publications, or supporting extension and outreach activities. Why Join Iowa State University? This position has served as a launching point for many early-career turfgrass professionals. Former Research Scientists have gone on to earn master's and doctoral degrees or build successful careers in the turfgrass industry. You'll have opportunities to lead applied research projects, present your work, contribute to publications, and develop the technical expertise needed for the next stage of your career. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. The selected candidate will be hired as a Research Scientist I. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: July 22, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19637 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Environmental-Systems-Mechanic-II_R19617": {
      "title": "Environmental Systems Mechanic II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Environmental Systems Mechanic II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Six years of experience in temperature and computerized building environmental automation systems, refrigeration or air conditioning work, including apprenticeship, or has two years of experience in computerized building environmental automation systems and meets the minimum eligibility requirements of ESM I; or four years experience in above plus Journeyman’s license; and • Has refrigeration certificate of at least type 2. • May need to possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. • Prefer 2 years of college/trade school. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Iowa State University is hiring an Environmental Systems Mechanic II to help maintain heating, cooling, and ventilation systems across student housing. This is a full time, steady position offering a variety of hands on HVAC work, including preventative maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs across residence halls and apartment communities. You will work both independently and as part of a skilled trades team to keep building systems operating safely and efficiently. With a variety of buildings and equipment, each day brings new challenges while still offering a consistent schedule and a supportive team environment. Schedule: Monday through Friday, 7:30AM to 4:00PM., with participation in an on call rotation. What you’ll do: Maintain and repair heating, cooling, ventilation, and refrigeration systems Troubleshoot system issues, including air balancing, steam systems, and equipment controls Calibrate thermostats, sensors, and other electronic control components Perform preventative maintenance and complete daily work orders Respond to HVAC related service calls and resolve issues efficiently What to expect in this role: Full time, on campus position supporting student housing facilities. Participation in an on call rotation to assist with after hours needs. Work in a variety of environments, including mechanical rooms and residential spaces. Physical, hands on work with exposure to varying temperatures, noise, and equipment. Why work with the Department of Residence: At Iowa State, the Department of Residence supports over 10,000 students across residence halls and apartment communities. Our facilities team plays an essential role in creating safe, comfortable living environments that support student success. In this position, you will gain experience working across a wide range of systems and spaces, offering variety in your day while maintaining a predictable schedule. You will be part of a dependable team that values collaboration, communication, and high quality work. Iowa State offers competitive pay and a comprehensive benefits package starting on your first day, including health insurance, paid time off, retirement programs, and tuition assistance. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5091a Original Posting Date: July 16, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19617 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Electrician-I_R19721": {
      "title": "Electrician I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Requires State of Iowa Class A or B Journeyman Electrician license. • Must possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Description: The Facilities Planning and Management department is seeking a journey level electrician to apply knowledge and skills to install and repair electrical systems to support operations of the Power Plant .  Preferred Qualifications Experience reading blueprints and electrical schematics Experience installing, maintaining, and repairing Utility electrical systems.  Experience working electrical maintenance in utility plant or process plant environment. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces electrical systems and electrical operated equipment (generally less than 600V), including but not limited to circuit breakers, relays, switches, wiring, conduit, receptacles, and magnetic starters and controls. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces electrical equipment, including but not limited to electric motors, transformers, generators, lights, fixtures, bulbs, tubes, motor control systems and meters. • Draws layouts, reads and interprets blueprints, schematics and other drawings. • As required, estimates materials needed and records time and materials expended on each work order. • Performs preventive maintenance on electrical equipment and systems. • Requires the knowledge of and ability to interpret local, state and national electrical codes. • Requires the ability to interpret instructions, design specifications and blueprints. • Perform other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the principles, methods and techniques used in the electrical trade. • Knowledge of the tools and equipment of the electrical trade and skill in their safe use. • Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade. • Knowledge of safety precautions mandated by OSHA, NFPA, NEC, and the EPA. • Knowledge of and ability to interpret local, state and national electrical codes. • Ability to interpret instructions, specifications and blueprints. • Ability to plan and perform work involving the installation, modification, troubleshooting and repair of new and existing electrical systems, and related equipment. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. • Ability to work outdoors in all types of weather conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. • Ability to work independently during normal work hours and after hours. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5071a Original Posting Date: August 11, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 7, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19721 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
