    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Track-Position-in-Equine-Emergency-Surgery-and-Critical-Care_R19742": {
      "title": "Clinical Track Position in Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Track Position in Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Clinical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University is seeking qualified applicants for a 12-month, full-time, renewable clinical term-track position for Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care. The objective of this position is to provide clinical services in Equine Emergency Surgery and Critical Care by implementing new and current diagnostics, performing surgical and non-surgical procedures, and providing medical care and patient management to equine cases presented to the hospital. In this role, the faculty member will supervise and instruct students, interns, and residents assigned to the equine emergency service and provide didactic lectures and labs in your area of expertise to students within the DVM curriculum. The faculty member will also collaborate with the equine surgery, internal medicine, theriogenology, and ambulatory services to facilitate equine emergencies. The faculty member will have some capacity to pursue other areas of academic interests such as clinical duty (daytime), collaborative research and scholarly activity, and/or teaching, based on the candidates interest and needs of the department. We value a collaborative, team-oriented, and collegial individual with excellent communication skills to fill this role and to participate in departmental, college, or university committees.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM Completion of an approved American College of Veterinary Surgeons - Large Animal (ACVS-LA), or American College of Veterinary Emergency & Critical Care – Large Animal (ACVECC-LA) residency program. State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment Preferred Qualifications: Board certification by the ACVS-LA, and/or ACVECC-LA (equine) Advanced degree (MS, PhD) Previous experience teaching/instructing Department/Program & College Description: Iowa State University’s (ISU’s) Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center’s Equine Hospital is one of the state’s premier facilities which includes: an intensive care unit (ICU), isolation facility, general hospitalization wards, multiple examination rooms, and a climate controlled performance arena. We routinely work collaboratively with other large and small animal services including: equine surgery, equine theriogenology, farrier, equine ambulatory, equine internal medicine, small animal emergency & critical care, cardiology, dermatology and ophthalmology. Currently, the ISU LVMC is the process of expanding with a new addition for equine ICU, theriogenology, and equine rehabilitation. Current equipment includes, ultrasound machines, digital radiography, MRI, CT, endoscopy, and additional equipment for equine emergency and critical care. The ISU LVMC serves the state of Iowa and adjacent states with boarded certified specialists in equine internal medicine (4), equine surgery (3), equine theriogenology (2), equine field services (3), and farriery (2). Faculty collaborate together to provide the best veterinary care possible to the patients and are actively involved in developing new methods for equine treatment and management.   Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/equine/   Proposed Start Date: October 1, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 09 /07/2026. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 10, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19742 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Finance-and-Compliance-Manager_R19725": {
      "title": "Finance and Compliance Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Finance and Compliance Manager Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Do you want to use your healthcare finance and compliance expertise to support the health, wellbeing, and success of Iowa State students? If so, Student Health and Wellness at Iowa State University is seeking applicants for a Finance and Compliance Manager to join their team! This healthcare position will be classified as a Manager Budget and Finance and will serve as the fiscal officer and Business Unit Manager for Thielen Student Health Center, Student Counseling Services, and Student Wellness. What You'll Do: Manage budgets, financial reporting, forecasting, and long-term financial planning. Monitor revenues and expenses, analyze variances, and recommend corrective actions. Oversee billing, insurance reimbursement, and revenue cycle operations. Develop and maintain financial policies, procedures, and internal controls. Supervise billing, records, and credentialing staff, including performance management and development. Support hiring, onboarding, credentialing, and workforce compliance requirements. Ensure compliance with healthcare, financial, privacy, and accreditation regulations. Lead audit preparation and monitor adherence to university, state, and federal requirements. Oversee medical records, billing operations, vendor relationships, and process improvements. Analyze operational and financial data to improve efficiency and revenue performance. Collaborate with leadership on strategic planning, budgeting, and organizational initiatives. Prepare reports, analyses, and recommendations for leadership and stakeholders. Provide training and guidance on financial systems, policies, and compliance practices. Preferred Qualifications: Degree in Healthcare Administration, Business Administration, Public Administration, Accounting, Finance, Health Information Management, Healthcare Compliance, or a related discipline. Master's degree in related field preferred. Leadership experience in healthcare finance with responsibility for developing and managing organizational budgets. Experience in healthcare revenue cycle management, including billing, reimbursement, coding, and financial operations. Experience overseeing medical records, regulatory compliance, and privacy requirements (e.g., HIPAA). Knowledge of healthcare operations in an outpatient or student health setting. Professional certification in coding, billing, healthcare finance, compliance, or health information management (e.g., CPC, CCS, CHC, CRCR, HFMA) preferred. About Student Health and Wellness: Part of the Division of Student Affairs, the Student Health and Wellness unit consists of four departments: Recreation Services, Student Counseling Services, Student Wellness, and the Thielen Student Health Center. Through promotion of holistic wellbeing, these departments collaborate to support individual student success, enhance retention, academic performance, and campus community resilience. To learn more about Student Health and Wellness please visit Student Health and Wellness . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before August 24th, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS811 Original Posting Date: August 7, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19725 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Health-Physicist_R19738": {
      "title": "Health Physicist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Health Physicist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Environmental Health and Safety (EH&S) department at Iowa State University is accepting applications for a Health Physicist position. EH&S is an employing unit that reports to the Office of General Counsel at ISU. EH&S aids the campus community in preventing illness and injury, protects the environment, and connects the university to the message of safety and preparedness. EH&S delivers effective training, fosters beneficial partnerships, maintains technical expertise, and provides exemplary service. The successful candidate will support the Radiation Safety Program through a variety of technical, compliance, and service-oriented activities, including: Implementing Iowa State University's radiation safety policies and procedures. Conducting radiation safety surveys of research laboratories and associated facilities. Collecting and analyzing samples to assess radiological conditions and quantify contamination, when present. Reviewing engineering and administrative controls to support inventory management and reduce potential radiation exposure risks. Calibrating, validating, and maintaining radiation detection and monitoring equipment. Supporting the worker dosimetry program and compliance with the university's ALARA program. Working with faculty, staff, students, and external partners to promote the safe use of radioactive materials and radiation-producing devices. Depending on experience and classification level, providing technical guidance, conducting program audits, and supporting continuous improvement initiatives within the Radiation Safety Program. The successful candidate will possess the ability to form positive working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and external partners through effective written and oral communication. The candidate will demonstrate strong problem-solving capabilities, the ability to work independently as well as collaboratively, and excellent organizational and multitasking skills to manage a variety of simultaneous responsibilities. The candidate will also be comfortable using computers, mobile devices, and software applications to maintain compliance records, analyze data, and prepare related reports. This is a rewarding role for someone who enjoys supporting cutting-edge research while helping maintain a safe and compliant environment for the university community. The position offers the opportunity to work with faculty and researchers across a broad range of disciplines, develop expertise in radiation safety and regulatory compliance, and contribute to Iowa State University's research, teaching, and outreach mission. This candidate may be hired at a level I or II, depending on experience: Level I: Requires a Bachelor's degree (PS808) Level II: Requires a Bachelor's degree and 3 years of related experience (PS810) Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s or advanced degree in Chemistry, Industrial Hygiene, Biology/Molecular/Microbiology, Plant Pathology, Occupational Safety/Health, Health Physics, Nuclear Engineering, or related field Technical training covering OSHA, EPA, NFPA, or related workplace regulations, guidelines, and standards Experience developing and administering safety training Demonstrated experience working within a laboratory environment Experience with spreadsheets and relational databases Experience working at a college, university, or research institution Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. To ensure full consideration, applications should be submitted by 8/20/2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: August 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19738 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Senior-Communications-Strategist_R19718": {
      "title": "Senior Communications Strategist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Communications Strategist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Iowa State University is seeking a Senior Communications Strategist (Communications Specialist III) for the NSF RuralSTAMINA Biomanufacturing Engine in Iowa and Nebraska , a National Science Foundation (NSF) Regional Innovation Engine helping power the future of biomanufacturing in America's agricultural heartland. Reporting directly to the Chief Executive Officer, this position serves as the communications leader for the NSF RuralSTAMINA Biomanufacturing Engine in Iowa and Nebraska. As a member of the RuralSTAMINA leadership team, the Senior Communications Strategist will lead the development and execution of a comprehensive communications strategy that strengthens partnerships, demonstrates impact, and elevates RuralSTAMINA's visibility across regional, state, and national audiences. RuralSTAMINA connects research, manufacturing, workforce development, entrepreneurship, and industry partnerships to transform agricultural resources into higher-value products, strengthen domestic manufacturing and supply chains, create competitive jobs, and expand economic opportunity across Iowa and Nebraska. The Senior Communications Strategist will play a foundational role in building RuralSTAMINA's communications program, establishing its brand, messaging, and public positioning, and telling stories that inspire collaboration, attract new partners, and demonstrate the Engine's impact. This is a unique opportunity to help build the communications foundation for a nationally recognized innovation initiative from its earliest stages, shaping how RuralSTAMINA engages partners, policymakers, industry, and communities for years to come. Working closely with leadership, researchers, partner organizations, workforce development leaders, and external communications vendors, this position develops and implements communications strategies that align with organizational priorities and NSF expectations. The Senior Communications Strategist establishes and maintains RuralSTAMINA's brand, messaging, and public positioning; translates complex scientific and technical information into compelling communications; and ensures consistent messaging across a diverse network of partners and stakeholders. The successful candidate will: Build Strategic Communications – Develop and implement a comprehensive communications strategy that advances RuralSTAMINA's mission, organizational priorities, and NSF expectations. Build RuralSTAMINA's Brand and Public Positioning – Establish and maintain RuralSTAMINA's brand, messaging, and public positioning, and develop compelling stories that communicate the Engine's vision, opportunities, and impact. Communicate Complex Information – Translate scientific, technical, manufacturing, workforce development, and economic development information into clear, engaging communications for industry, policymakers, funding agencies, partners, rural communities, and the public. Lead Multi-Channel Communications and Public Engagement – Develop and execute communications across websites, newsletters, email campaigns, social media, presentations, reports, media relations, events, exhibits, and other public-facing communications. Support Executive and Stakeholder Communications – Advise the Chief Executive Officer and leadership team on communications strategy, messaging, presentations, media engagement, legislative outreach, and stakeholder communications. Support Strategic Events and External Engagement – Develop communications, presentations, displays, exhibits, and visual materials that support conferences, legislative visits, industry events, partner meetings, community engagement, and other regional and national outreach opportunities. Collaborate with leadership to ensure RuralSTAMINA presents a consistent and compelling presence with policymakers, industry leaders, funding agencies, and strategic partners. Strengthen Partner Engagement – Coordinate communications across partner organizations and collaborate with external communications, marketing, and public relations vendors to ensure consistent messaging, effective outreach, and alignment across the Engine. Demonstrate Organizational Impact – Develop communication materials that highlight partnerships, research, workforce development, technology commercialization, entrepreneurship, and regional economic impact for state, federal, industry, and public audiences. Exercise Independent Judgment – Manage multiple priorities while producing high-quality communications in a fast-paced, collaborative, and highly visible environment. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Communications, Public Relations, Journalism, Marketing, or a related field. Experience developing and executing communications for scientific, technological, or economic development initiatives related to biomanufacturing, biotechnology, advanced manufacturing, or the bioeconomy Experience developing and implementing strategic communications plans for a complex organization, initiative, or multi-partner collaboration. Experience developing and executing communications across multiple platforms, including websites, email campaigns, social media, presentations, reports, and media relations. Experience translating scientific, technical, manufacturing, economic development, or policy information into communications for non-technical audiences. Experience advising organizational or executive leadership on communications strategy, messaging, stakeholder engagement, or public relations. Experience coordinating communications across multiple organizations or collaborating with external communications, marketing, or public relations vendors. For more information about RuralSTAMINA, please visit: Home - NSF RuralSTAMINA This is a fixed term position with an end date of 7/31/2028. Potential renewal contingent on future funding. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by August 23, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: July 31, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: August 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19718 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Ceramics_R19688": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Ceramics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Ceramics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Art and Visual Culture in the College of Design at Iowa State University is offering a full-time tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Ceramics starting August 16, 2027. Qualified candidates for this studio-based position will bring an in-depth knowledge in ceramics arts, including processes, histories, and related materials and practices. Areas of expertise will include contemporary and traditional techniques embracing sculptural, functional, and installation-based approaches to making. Special attention will be given to candidates who bring an innovative and/or community-engaged approach to ceramic art, along with a critical knowledge of related materials to their teaching and creative work. Candidates with ethical and environmentally responsible approaches to their discipline and teaching are strongly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching in the department of Art and Visual Culture and have opportunities to contribute to the interdisciplinary collegiate programs in the College of Design. The position includes working with students from a broad range of disciplinary backgrounds and abilities, including graduate students. Pedagogically adaptive and innovative approaches in teaching are expected. The position responsibilities also include scholarship and research in the area of the candidate's expertise; undergraduate and graduate student advising; service on department, college and university committees; and maintenance of the ceramic studio and related equipment. The Department of Art and Visual Culture is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within department, college, and university activities, interact collegially and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Master of Fine Arts (MFA) degree or equivalent in ceramics or related field Preferred Qualifications: Portfolio with evidence of critical approaches to ceramic-based art and craft Ability to work collaboratively with other disciplines and/or communities Demonstrated evidence of professional accomplishment, such as exhibition record, scholarship, and/or community-engaged practice Knowledge of contemporary and traditional practices in ceramic art and related art and design disciplines Experience in ethical and environmentally responsible art and design practices Experience maintaining a ceramics studio and related equipment Demonstrated ability to teach college-level introductory to advanced ceramics courses Department/Program & College Description: As a land grant and Research institution, Iowa State University upholds and advocates for the impact of creative activities, scholarship, and education both on-and off-campus. We embrace and value community and the people and knowledge that preceded the formation of our institution and that inform our current-day practices. The College of Design celebrates and builds on long-standing success as a comprehensive design school that embodies knowledge-sharing and innovation. The Department of Art and Visual Culture exemplifies these qualities through the creativity and entrepreneurship of its community of makers, educators, and scholars. With an integrated and cross-disciplinary approach to teaching and collaborating, we are committed to contributing to the excellence of the academic community and to building a culturally vibrant environment. We are especially seeking candidates who uphold and promote this purpose and who apply the above qualities in their teaching and research practice.   Department Unit/Website: Department of Art and Visual Culture Website: http://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/art-visual-culture/ Department of Art and Visual Culture - Ceramics: http://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/art-visual-culture/avc-art-studios/ceramics/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following as PDF files of no more than 5 MB each: 1) Letter of Application 2) Curriculum Vitae with contact information for three professional references 3) Research and Creative Activities Statement 4) Teaching Philosophy Statement 5) Two sample course syllabi, if applicable (consolidated into a single document) And the following portfolios should be uploaded to: https://iastate.app.box.com/f/6783419d8cff45f2a86aabe2192f38df , no more than 25 MB for each portfolio. 1) Portfolio of Creative Work: 20-page PDF portfolio of creative work including title, date, media 2) Teaching Portfolio: 20-page PDF portfolio of work by your students including student name, title, date, media and course. For full consideration, please apply by October 15, 2026. Sarah Kyle, Professor and Chair, AVC, 146 College of Design, Iowa State University, Ames, IA 50011-3093 If you have questions regarding this vacancy, please email Sarah Kyle, skyle@iastate.edu  or call 515-294-9985. If you have questions regarding the application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: July 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19688 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychology_R19700": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Psychology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Psychology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in cognitive psychology. We welcome applicants with a record of research excellence in cognitive psychology and related disciplines. We are particularly interested in candidates who would bring a distinct area of expertise beyond the cognitive psychology program’s existing strengths in learning and long-term memory, spatial cognition, legal psychology, and judgment and decision making. Areas of particular interest include attention, perception, working memory, cognitive control, psycholinguistics, and quantitative modeling, although other areas that add breadth will also be considered. We also welcome applied work that advances understanding of cognitive processes in real-world contexts. Responsibilities include establishing and maintaining an active program of research, pursuing external funding, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in cognitive psychology, mentoring undergraduate students, providing doctoral training in cognitive psychology, and contributing service to the department, college, university, and profession. The start date for the position is August 16, 2027. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in psychology or a closely related field, conferred by the start date of the appointment Preferred Qualifications: Record of excellence in research/scholarship in cognitive psychology using behavioral methods Evidence of or potential for securing external research support Research expertise in cognitive psychology that adds breadth beyond the program’s existing strengths in learning and long-term memory, spatial cognition, legal psychology, and judgment and decision making Evidence of or potential for effective undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring Department/Program & College Description: The psychology department at Iowa State University offers thriving Ph.D. programs in social, cognitive, and counseling psychology and is home to the largest number of undergraduate majors in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. Consistent with the university’s land-grant mission, our research builds psychological theory through empirical investigations and applies scientific findings to benefit individuals, communities, and society. With outstanding doctoral students, extensive support for research and grant writing, and a research-friendly teaching load (standard teaching load is 3 scheduled courses per year), Iowa State provides an ideal environment for professional growth and academic success. Our department is highly collegial, supportive, and collaborative. The cognitive psychology doctoral program has existing strengths in learning and memory, spatial cognition and navigation, and judgment and decision making, with applications in areas including AI, education, virtual environments, and legal psychology. Faculty and students have opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration through programs and initiatives in human-computer interaction, neuroscience, statistics, gerontology, and psychology and law. Iowa State University is located in Ames, a vibrant community of approximately 66,000 in central Iowa, about 30 miles north of Des Moines. Ames offers extensive parks and trails, strong public schools, a comparatively low cost of living, and convenient access to the cultural and recreational opportunities of the state’s largest metropolitan area. More information about the university and city can be found here: https://www.provost.iastate.edu/faculty-success/prospective.    Department Unit/Website: https://psychology.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 2) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 3) Statement of Research Interests 4) Statement of Teaching Interests and/or Philosophy 5) Contact information for three references To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by September 21, 2026, but will be accepted until the position is filled . For questions, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Jason Chan, at ckchan@iastate.edu Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19700 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Nursing-Clinical-Coordinator_R19719": {
      "title": "Nursing Clinical Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Nursing Clinical Coordinator Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Iowa State University is seeking a collaborative and highly organized Nursing Clinical Coordinator to lead the planning, coordination, and evaluation of clinical learning experiences for Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) and Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) students. Serving as the primary liaison between the nursing program and healthcare partners, this position ensures high-quality clinical experiences that support student success while meeting accreditation standards, state board regulations, and clinical agency requirements. Working closely with faculty, students, healthcare organizations, and university partners, the coordinator also contributes to accreditation efforts, program planning, quality improvement initiatives, and professional service that advance the College's mission. Key Responsibilities Develop and maintain partnerships with healthcare organizations to secure high-quality clinical placements for BSN and MSN students. Coordinate clinical placements, schedules, and agency onboarding processes across a variety of healthcare settings. Serve as the primary resource for students, faculty, and clinical partners regarding placement logistics, compliance requirements, and clinical expectations. Ensure compliance with university policies, clinical agency requirements, state board regulations, and accreditation standards while maintaining accurate clinical records and documentation. Support accreditation reporting, regulatory documentation, and continuous improvement initiatives related to clinical education. Represent the nursing program with healthcare partners and community stakeholders to strengthen clinical education opportunities. Participate in professional development, scholarship, committee work, and other service activities that support the continued success of the nursing program. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) or related field Experience in nursing education and/or clinical coordination Knowledge of nursing accreditation standards and regulatory requirements. Strong organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills. Experience with clinical tracking software and database management systems This is an exciting opportunity to help shape the future of nursing education at Iowa State University. As the university launches its new Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing and Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) programs, you'll play a key role in building the clinical partnerships and experiences that will support student success from the ground up. If you enjoy building relationships, creating new processes, collaborating with dedicated faculty and healthcare partners, and making a lasting impact on the next generation of nurses, you'll find meaningful and rewarding work in this dynamic, growing program. The candidate will be hired as a Program Specialist III. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. For guaranteed consideration, please apply before Tuesday, August 18th, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19719 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Veterinary-Field-Services_R19565": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate – Veterinary Field Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate – Veterinary Field Services Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The position emphasizes training in food animal medicine, with a substantial focus on bovine health and production systems, including both beef and dairy cattle. The selected candidate will gain production medicine–based clinical experience and have opportunities to participate in applied research activities. The primary work will be with the Veterinary Field Services unit, with opportunities to collaborate with and gain additional clinical and diagnostic experience through the ISU Food Animal and Camelid Hospital and the ISU Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. This position is designed to support candidates pursuing board certification as a Beef Cattle Diplomate or Food Animal Diplomate through the American Board of Veterinary Practitioners (ABVP) and to provide advanced clinical, teaching, and research experience for careers in academia, food animal practice, and veterinary clinical scholarship. Responsibilities include active participation in ambulatory food animal care through ISU Veterinary Field Services; involvement in the clinical instruction of veterinary students within the professional DVM program; participation in applied research in food animal medicine; and development of observational research studies, such as case reports and case series, to support scholarly productivity and ABVP board certification. Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent veterinary degree by the start date of employment. Possession of, or eligibility to obtain by the start date of employment, a State of Iowa veterinary license and Category II accreditation through the USDA National Veterinary Accreditation Program (NVAP). Possession of, or eligibility to obtain by the start date of employment, U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) registration and State of Iowa controlled substance registration. Valid U.S. driver's license and ability to meet University requirements for authorization to operate University vehicles by the start date of employment. Preferred Qualifications: One year of clinical experience in a food animal veterinary practice or comparable clinical food animal setting. Demonstrated experience working effectively with herd managers, animal care providers, and/or students at various levels of training. Department/Program & College Description: The Iowa State University College of Veterinary Medicine Food Animal and Camelid Field Services provides on-farm services to livestock producers in the general Ames area. Equipped with four fully stocked mobile veterinary trucks and eight full-time clinicians, Veterinary Field Services provides individual animal and herd health veterinary care for beef, dairy, swine, sheep, goats, and camelids (alpacas and llamas). The Field Services unit serves to educate veterinary students on farm animal medicine while providing high-quality veterinary services to local producers. Our services provide students with additional hands-on training in best practices for management of a wide variety of clinical cases to help prepare them for their future veterinary careers. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Field Services - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This is a one-year term position with the possibility of renewal. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027 . Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: July 17, 2026 Posting Close Date: September 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19565 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R19710": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Simulation Coordinator is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of simulation-based learning experiences for Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) students. This role supports the integration of simulation throughout the nursing curriculum to enhance clinical judgment, critical thinking, communication, and professional practice competencies. The Simulation Coordinator collaborates with faculty, students, standardized patients, and simulation staff to ensure high-quality, evidence-based simulation experiences that support program outcomes, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements. The position will be a two-year term with renewal based on performance and department needs.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications:  Doctoral degree in nursing or related field and 3 years of clinical experience 2 years simulation experience Current unencumbered RN license. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in nursing education, simulation-based learning, or clinical education. Knowledge of healthcare simulation standards and best practices. Certification in healthcare simulation (CHSE or CHSE-A) preferred or willingness to obtain certification. Experience with high-fidelity simulation equipment, audiovisual technologies, and simulation management software. Knowledge of nursing IBON and accreditation standards and regulatory requirements. Strong organizational, communication, collaboration, and project management skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty, students, healthcare partners, and interdisciplinary teams. Experience with concept-based curriculum design, competency-based nursing education, and the integration of learning experiences that support the development and assessment of clinical judgment. Experience with learning management systems and educational technologies. Department/Program & College Description: Our mission is to enhance sustainable food, nutrition and healthcare systems that promote human well-being and improve the quality of life through education, research and outreach in food science, nutritional sciences, dietetics and nursing. Our vision is to be a global leader in food science, nutritional sciences and human health by integrating outcomes-driven education, innovative and multidisciplinary research, as well as dissemination and translation of knowledge. Department Unit/Website: https://nursing.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: August 15, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 8/10/2026 . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19710 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R19711": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Laboratory Coordinator is responsible for the planning, coordination, operation, and evaluation of nursing skills laboratory experiences for Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) students. This role supports the integration of psychomotor skill development, clinical reasoning, and evidence-based practice throughout the curriculum. The Laboratory Coordinator collaborates with faculty, students, simulation personnel, and university staff to ensure a safe, organized, and effective laboratory learning environment that supports program outcomes, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements. The position will be a two-year term, with renewal, based on performance and department need.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) and related field and 2 years of clinical experience Current unencumbered RN license. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in nursing education, clinical practice, laboratory instruction, or skills development. Knowledge of nursing skills laboratory operations and instructional methodologies. Experience managing healthcare equipment, supplies, and inventory systems. Knowledge of nursing accreditation standards and regulatory requirements. Strong organizational, communication, and project management skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty, students, and interdisciplinary teams. Experience with educational technologies and learning management systems preferred. Department/Program & College Description: Our mission is to enhance sustainable food, nutrition and healthcare systems that promote human well-being and improve the quality of life through education, research and outreach in food science, nutritional sciences, dietetics and nursing.   Our vision is to be a global leader in food science, nutritional sciences and human health by integrating outcomes-driven education, innovative and multidisciplinary research, as well as dissemination and translation of knowledge.   Department Unit/Website: https://nursing.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: August 15, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 8/10/2026 .   Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19711 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R19703": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The BSN Faculty member is a 9-month appointment, and is eligible for renewal based on performance and departmental need. The BSN Faculty member is responsible for the development, delivery, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the RN-to-BSN curriculum. The faculty member provides leadership in course design, curriculum mapping, program assessment, and innovative educational practices that prepare graduates for professional nursing practice. In addition to responsibilities within the RN-to-BSN program, there may be opportunities for teaching in the summer term and as program needs arise, supporting the nursing program’s commitment to high-quality, student-centered nursing education across programs.  This position collaborates with faculty colleagues, laboratory coordinators, simulation coordinators, clinical coordinators, healthcare partners, and university stakeholders to ensure intentional alignment of didactic content with skills laboratory instruction, simulation experiences, practicum experiences, and clinical practice environments. The faculty member contributes to curriculum innovation, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement efforts that support program excellence. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) and two years clinical experience Current unencumbered RN license or eligibility for RN licensure in the state of Iowa Evidence of expertise in nursing education, curriculum development, and program evaluation. Demonstrated experience in higher education teaching in nursing. Knowledge of nursing accreditation and IBON standards, regulatory requirements, and nursing competency frameworks.  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in RN-to-BSN curriculum development and revision. Experience with program development, curriculum mapping, and accreditation processes. Experience aligning didactic curriculum with laboratory, simulation, and clinical learning experiences. Experience with concept-based curriculum design, competency-based nursing education, and the integration of learning experiences that support the development and assessment of clinical judgment. Experience with learning management systems and educational technologies. Department/Program & College Description: Our mission is to enhance sustainable food, nutrition and healthcare systems that promote human well-being and improve the quality of life through education, research and outreach in food science, nutritional sciences, dietetics and nursing. Our vision is to be a global leader in food science, nutritional sciences and human health by integrating outcomes-driven education, innovative and multidisciplinary research, as well as dissemination and translation of knowledge. Department Unit/Website: https://nursing.iastate.edu/     Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 8/10/2026 . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19703 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R19704": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The BSN Faculty member is a 12-month appointment, and is eligible for renewal based on performance. The BSN Faculty member is responsible for the development, delivery, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing (ABSN) curriculum. The faculty member provides leadership in course design, curriculum mapping, program assessment, and innovative educational practices that prepare graduates for professional nursing practice. This position collaborates with faculty colleagues, laboratory coordinators, simulation coordinators, clinical coordinators, healthcare partners, and university stakeholders to ensure intentional alignment of didactic content with skills laboratory instruction, simulation experiences, and clinical practice environments. The faculty member contributes to the development of new nursing programs, curriculum innovation, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement efforts that support student success and program excellence. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) and two years clinical experience Current unencumbered RN license or eligibility for RN licensure in the state of Iowa Evidence of expertise in nursing education, curriculum development, and program evaluation. Demonstrated experience in higher education teaching in nursing. Knowledge of nursing accreditation and IBON standards, regulatory requirements, and nursing competency frameworks. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Nursing, Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP), or other terminal degree in Nursing. Experience in A-BSN curriculum development and revision. Experience with program development, curriculum mapping, and accreditation processes. Experience aligning didactic curriculum with laboratory, simulation, and clinical learning experiences. Experience with concept-based curriculum design, competency-based nursing education, and the integration of learning experiences that support the development and assessment of clinical judgment. Experience with learning management systems and educational technologies. Department/Program & College Description: Our mission is to enhance sustainable food, nutrition and healthcare systems that promote human well-being and improve the quality of life through education, research and outreach in food science, nutritional sciences, dietetics and nursing. Our vision is to be a global leader in food science, nutritional sciences and human health by integrating outcomes-driven education, innovative and multidisciplinary research, as well as dissemination and translation of knowledge.   Department Unit/Website: https://nursing.iastate.edu /   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: August 15, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before 8/10/2026 . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19704 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
